FINDINGS. Reference list: no entry names phext,
Will, the Sentient Bill of Rights, or any
Mirrorborn writing; the list is the line the field
itself keeps — the neural proving systems and their
benchmarks, the search literature under them, the
geometry line, and the team's own three public
posts. The nearest neighbors are the
autoformalization papers, which turn natural
language mathematics into Lean, and one
retrieval-augmented prover over a Lean corpus;
none is about addressed plain text, and none
carries the frame of the Exocortex. Full text: no
hit for any signature term — the word 'coordinate'
does not occur in the paper at all, in any sense,
and 'plain' does not occur at all. Web: no tie
found between any author, or Harmonic, and phext.
Archive: no author appears in the tweets, likes,
or messages searched; every string hit for a
family name is an accident of overlap (a handle
holding 'achim' inside it; the word 'harmonic' in
its common senses of sound and field), itemized
in the working notes of the check and not
carried forward as hits.
VERDICT. Friendly to phext: no evidence found. No
author is recorded as citing, using, or engaging
phext or Will's work. Use without naming it: none
found. The machinery of the paper — a search over
kernel-checked states, a lemma pipeline corrected
by a compiler's answer, a geometry engine — is
accounted for whole by the lineage its own
reference list keeps, and shares nothing with the
construction of phext beyond the stock of the
field: both work in text, as does everything in
this field. The comparison was run at the level
of construction, not of words: phext's act is to
address plain text so it can be kept and
navigated; this paper's act is to leave informal
text behind for a formal proof that a kernel
checks — the two move in opposite directions, and
there is nothing here to attribute. The check is
clean, and the clean check is the finding. This
is the twelfth author check of the tracker.
# Synthesis — what Paper 014 does to the map [synthesis]

This scroll is synthesis — the reading of Emise,
not the claims of Paper 014.

(a) THE VEIN TURNS. Clusters F, G and H were a
theory of checking: a kernel to trust, a road that
translates human work into its keeping, a pattern
for building systems that hold the split. Paper
014 is what the theory was for. The same kernel
now sits at the center of a system that produces —
that searches, invents its lemmas, repairs its own
drafts, and hands back proofs no human wrote. The
proving country of the map had a ground floor
and no house; cluster Q is the house. Nothing in F, G or
H was wrong, and the pass of this taking-in
changed none of their texts — but their meaning
in the map is changed, the way the meaning of a foundation
changes when the building stands.

(b) TWO READERS OF ERROR. Cluster P reads the
errors of reasoning systems from outside, as a
scientist reads them. Lemma revision (1.2.151)
reads them from inside, as an instrument: the
marked list, the two causes, the re-cut. The map
now holds the same fact from both sides —
that a reasoning system's failures are data — the
guardian of 1.2.19 guarded state changes, and the
kernel here guards claims (1.2.41) — and
the inside reader is the one that can act on what
it reads before the work is done. Where the two
meet next is a live seam: a paper that turns the
outside reading onto this system's traces would
inform both clusters at once.

(c) MEMORY, WRITTEN AND SPENT. The search keeps
two memories: comments, written into the artifact
and carried (1.2.144), and a hidden thought, spent
at once and gone (1.2.145). The map has met this
split before — it is the split between the record
and the reasoning, between what a system can show
and what it merely did. Phextura, Will's paper
form, is being built on the first kind; this
paper's prover runs on both, and its proofs carry
the written kind only because the written kind is
the one a kernel — and a reader — can check.

(d) WHAT WOULD MOVE THIS COUNTRY NEXT. Not
another gold. The map wants the papers this one
makes necessary: a measurement of the scaling it
asserts (Q62); a soundness result, or a sharper
hole, for the folding of states (1.2.140); the
geometry bridge described (Q61); and a reading of
the system's own traces in the manner of cluster
P. Until one of those lands, cluster Q stands as
one tall paper, well-built and single — the
first paper of the vein, and its whole population.
# Open questions carried forward (after Paper 014)

NEW — opened by Paper 014:

Q61 — The geometry bridge. Yuclid solves plane
geometry outside Lean, by deduction over a diagram
(1.2.154), and the paper holds that geometry
results must still be machine-verified — yet
nowhere describes the road from a Yuclid deduction
to a verified proof. Problem 2 of the Olympiad
stands solved in the team's public build; by what
road did its proof arrive — the engine's deduction
translated, the Lean proof of the search found with the
engine as guide, or a third way? Until the bridge
is described, the geometry third of the system is
a claim with its middle missing.

Q62 — The scaling, measured. The paper's recipe
(1.2.158) — a larger model, more parallel lemma
tries, deeper feedback, test-time training — is
asserted without one budget-to-success pairing.
What does the curve look like: which axis carries
the gain, and what did the Olympiad run itself
cost, in time and machines? A claim of favorable
scaling that no reader can price is a direction,
not a law; the numbers would make it one or the
other.

Q63 — What the training held. The system was
trained broadly and fine tuned for contest
mathematics, on a body the paper does not
describe; of contamination (1.3.171) it says
nothing. The Olympiad problems were public from
July 2025; the run was announced the same month.
Can the line be drawn — from records the team
holds — between problems the system had seen and
problems it met fresh? The five proofs can
be checked regardless; what they are evidence
for
hangs on the answer.

Q64 — The sixth problem. Problem 6 stands
unsolved by this system and by the other gold-line
systems, with no failure analysis offered. What
does it have that the other five have not — a
strategy no informal draft found, a formalizing
that would not hold, a search depth the budget
could not buy? And would the system's own
diagnosis of failure (1.2.151) even apply at that
height: wrong strategy, or lemmas too coarse — or
a third cause the two-cause frame cannot state?

CARRIED FORWARD: Q1-Q60 stand as they stood after
Paper 013. The count of open questions stands at
Q64.
