(1.3.225), and the defined words heteroscedastic
(1.3.227), unimodal (1.3.228), extremal (1.3.229).
Pointers only: this scroll makes no claim of its own.
# Paper 019 — Fast Computation of the Kippenhahn Hypersurface of a Joint Numerical Range (Rito)

Source: arXiv:2611.14543 (math.RA), version 1, submitted
24 October 2026. One author: Carlos Rito, of the Centro de
Matematica da Universidade do Minho (Polo CMAT-UTAD), Portugal,
financed by Portuguese funds through FCT within project
UID/00013/2025. The paper carries a disclosure of its making:
the original algorithm was written in Magma by the author, and
the Magma code was translated into Singular by ChatGPT 6, to
provide an implementation in open-source software. Read entire
in its HTML form, 2026-11-14.

THE THIRST. The twelfth paper of the Thirst (charter rule 17),
posted by Will in the MOAT chat with the HTML link, and the
first the stream has carried into computational algebraic
geometry. It was weighed blind under seal beforehand, like every
paper of the quest: the skim priced an abstract that lists its steps —
factor, test, sample, interpolate, lift, certify — at nine
concepts, no revision, no axis, Index 0.0367. The reading gave
eleven concepts in a new cluster; the score stands at 30.1.5.

THE DELTA. Eleven concepts, all founding cluster Y
(1.2.237-1.2.247): the joint numerical range (1.2.237); the
determinantal polynomial that carries it (1.2.238); the
algebraic Kippenhahn variety, the dual whose real part generates
the range (1.2.239); Katz's test, the gate that decides which factors have a hypersurface dual (1.2.240); the Gauss map
(1.2.241); sampling the dual over finite fields (1.2.242); the
candidate degree, found by the size of a kernel (1.2.243);
completely split primes (1.2.244); the reconstruction across the
roots, from finite fields back to the number field (1.2.245);
certification of the reconstruction (1.2.246); and the four
certified dual surfaces the method is proved on (1.2.247).
Eleven foundations (1.3.230-1.3.240) and three defined words
(1.3.241-1.3.243) carry the paper's terms at level zero. No held
concept is revised — the second paper running where the revision
stands priced at zero in the seal and lands at zero. Three
questions open (Q97-Q99); Q84 is informed, not closed. The
