Addendum 2026-11-09 (Paper 008). Six new canonical concepts
stand in Section 2: the Arnold number and the strong Arnold
conjecture (1.2.98), clean maps and the perturbation bound
(1.2.99), the Arnold number of a group (1.2.100), stretching
films (1.2.101), flag varieties and Crit = dim + 1 (1.2.102),
and the floor that stands (1.2.103). Cluster assignments:
all six to cluster E (the symplectic wing, extended above).
Canonical concept count is now 103. Standoff map for the
new concepts: the fixed point and the Hamiltonian
diffeomorphism (1.3.118), the critical point (1.3.119), the
flag and the Grassmannian (1.3.120), and the eigenvalue
(1.3.121) are level zero for Paper 008; symplectic (1.3.22),
and maps between spaces
(1.3.16) hold the older ground under the new; homology
(1.3.13) and the symplectic area rule are the shared
ground of the two Floer roads, at each other's side
in 15.2.1.

Addendum 2026-11-09 (Paper 009). Six new canonical
concepts (1.2.104-1.2.109), no held concept revised,
cluster N founded — celestial mechanics: the segment
problem. Canonical concept count is now 109. No
restructuring pass fell due at this taking-in (the next
falls at Paper 010 or 120 concepts; 109 stands under both
triggers). Standoff map for the new concepts: flow and
trajectory (1.3.124), gravitational potential (1.3.125),
angular momentum (1.3.126), and cone (1.3.127) are level
zero, new with this paper; the fixed point and the
Hamiltonian diffeomorphism (1.3.118) and symplectic
(1.3.22) carry the bridge to cluster E; invariant (1.3.5)
and the state machine (1.3.85) frame the cone and the
machines of 16.1.2.

Addendum 2026-11-09 (Paper 010). Seven new canonical
concepts (1.2.110-1.2.116), no held concept revised,
cluster O founded — statistics: judging a model from
logged data. Canonical concept count is now 116.
RESTRUCTURE PASS #6 ran at this taking-in
(every-5-papers trigger; record above). Standoff map
for the new concepts: chance and probability (1.3.129),
a sample and independence (1.3.130), expectation
(1.3.131), risk (1.3.132), the estimator and consistency
(1.3.133), the bandit table (1.3.134), the importance
weight (1.3.135), gradient descent (1.3.136), growing
together (1.3.137), the bell law (1.3.138), and the index
(1.3.139) are level zero, new with this paper — the
largest single laying-down of foundations since the
layer was built; average and distribution (1.3.8),
generalization and domain shift (1.3.40), and the state
machine (1.3.85) frame the cluster from older ground.

Addendum (Paper 011). Cluster P is founded: reasoning
read through its errors — the failure side of the
capability territory of cluster A, read in the program
space of cluster I. Seven concepts (1.2.117-1.2.123).
Standoff map for cluster P: the synthesis stands on the
skeleton as specification (1.2.57) and follows the
measurement agenda (1.2.14); the comparison carries the revision of the
capability profile (1.2.4) and reads its witnesses
through the induced feature spaces of cluster B (1.2.28);
aliasing stands beside behavior and structure (1.2.60),
one case of a thing left open beside the other. The revision of
this paper reached back into cluster A, not forward into
new ground: the first paper of the Thirst to correct a
held scroll, and the correction is a pair of species
sharing one profile-space with two shapes of jaggedness.

Addendum (Paper 012). Cluster O is extended: the
pricing of estimators at the signal, beside the
pricing of rules from records — seven concepts
(1.2.124-1.2.130), one held concept revised (1.2.116,
the floor, gaining the rider of the price at a
signal). Standoff map for the extension: the sequence
model (1.3.145), projection onto a convex set
(1.3.146), the sharp rate (1.3.147), the proximal
step and the Moreau envelope (1.3.148), the Poincare
inequality (1.3.149), the tangent cone and
statistical dimension (1.3.150), and the monotone
cone (1.3.151) are level zero, new with this paper;
the bell law (1.3.138), a sample and independence
(1.3.130), expectation (1.3.131), and the estimator
(1.3.133) carry the ground of Paper 010 under the
new; the defined words proximal (1.3.152), isotonic
(1.3.153), ellipsoid (1.3.154) and variational
(1.3.155) are coined for the extension. The
extension stands inside the own bridges of the
cluster:
the decomposition reads measure, then change
(cluster M) at the scale of one place, and its split
is the top-p move (cluster J) at the scale of one
price. No restructuring pass fell due at this
taking-in (the next falls at Paper 015 or 140
concepts; the count stands at 130).

Addendum (Paper 013). Cluster O is extended again:
the pricing of the spread of a judging, beside the
pricing of rules from records and of estimators at
the signal — eight concepts (1.2.131-1.2.138), no
held concept revised. Standoff map for the
extension: cross-validation (1.3.156), a split, a
fold, and a partition (1.3.157), influence (1.3.158),
joint effects split by the sets that carry them
(1.3.159), pair scores (1.3.160), and the bell limit
(1.3.161) are level zero, new with this paper; a
sample and independence (1.3.130), the estimator
(1.3.133), expectation (1.3.131), average and spread
(1.3.8), the bell law (1.3.138), and the report card of the classifier
(1.3.38) carry the ground of Papers 010
and 012 under the new. No word was coined for the
extension: the paper's terms are the plain words of the field, and they stand in the foundations as they
stand. The extension stands inside the own bridges of the cluster, and adds one of its own: the dealing of
shares by the mass they carry reaches cluster J
(1.2.70) from 1.2.131, and the audit of the reading of a grade
reaches cluster A (1.2.14) from 1.2.138. No
restructuring pass fell due at this taking-in (the
next falls at Paper 015 or 140 concepts; the count
stands at 138).

Addendum (Paper 018). Cluster O is extended a third
time: the pricing of how an estimator stands up to hard
noise — seven concepts (1.2.230-1.2.236), no held
concept revised. The test that prices a candidate, and
the l_1-estimator it defines; extremal elements and
their degree; the average-moment price; the coincidence
on the monotone class; the sign step; the loud point;
weighted hearing on a line. Standoff map for the
extension: spread that changes from place to place
(1.3.222), a heavy tail (1.3.223), the sign of a number
(1.3.224), one peak (1.3.225), and cutting power
(1.3.226) are level zero, new with this paper; the
sequence model (1.3.145), projection onto a convex set
(1.3.146), the monotone cone (1.3.151), the estimator
and consistency (1.3.133), the bell law (1.3.138), and
the slope-bounded law (1.3.149) carry the ground under
the new. Three words were coined for the extension:
heteroscedastic (1.3.227), unimodal (1.3.228), and
extremal (1.3.229). The extension stands on ground the
cluster already holds — the estimator of Paper 012 —
and draws two bridges out: to the measurement agenda
of cluster A, where hearing is a measurement choice,
and to the test-built specification of cluster I.

Addendum (Paper 014). A new cluster is founded:
Q — Automated theorem proving (Paper 014;
1.2.139-1.2.158), the system cluster of the proving vein, standing
on clusters F-H as a house
stands on its ground floor. Twenty concepts: the
search and its folding (1.2.139, 1.2.140); its law
and its choosing (1.2.141, 1.2.142); one model as
policy and value (1.2.143); the two
memories of the search (1.2.144, 1.2.145); the proof it hands
back (1.2.146); its three trainings (1.2.147,
1.2.148, 1.2.149); the lemma pipeline and its
revision (1.2.150, 1.2.151); what formalizing does
to error, and what the prover invents (1.2.152,
1.2.153); the geometry engine and its algebraic
tables (1.2.154, 1.2.155); the stateless engine
room (1.2.156); the standard of solved (1.2.157);
and the scaling recipe, with its evidence priced
(1.2.158). No held concept revised. Standoff map
for the founding: a proof state and a tactic
(1.3.162), Monte Carlo search (1.3.163), an
olympiad (1.3.164), a deductive database
(1.3.165), and sameness (1.3.166) are level zero,
new with this paper; and six words are coined and
defined (1.3.167-1.3.172): autoformalization,
counterexample, derangement, subgraph,
contamination, divisor. The founding stands wired:
down into cluster F (1.2.40, 1.2.41, 1.2.43),
across to cluster G (1.2.48) and cluster H
(1.2.53, 1.2.55, 1.2.56), and out to the guardian
of cluster B (1.2.19), the capability profile of
cluster A (1.2.14), the induced feature spaces of
cluster C (1.2.28), the informal check of cluster
I (1.2.63), the budget that follows the mass of
cluster J (1.2.70), and the error-reading of
cluster P (1.2.117-1.2.123). Restructure Pass #7
fell due inside this taking-in and stands logged
above; the next falls at Paper 015 or 160
concepts, the count standing at 158.

Addendum — Paper 015 (2026-11-11): cluster R
(1.2.159-1.2.170) — the statistical mechanics of language:
the thermalization hypothesis; words, particles,
households — one quantity in three tongues; two
conservation laws, one equilibrium; Rayleigh-Jeans
condensation; constraint-driven condensation; the reduced
frequency; the rare-word condensate; the density of states
as the model's free shape; a fit anchored to inequality;
three curves, one distribution; the Zipf window; wealth
thermalization. Links outward: 1.2.165 to cluster J
(1.2.70); 1.2.162 to cluster D (1.2.31); 1.2.163 to
cluster A (1.2.7); 1.2.160 to cluster C (1.2.24).
Restructure Pass #8 fell due inside this taking-in and
