We're going to provide users with a first-class upgrade from TEI-XML to Phextura. Using multiversal phext and standoff properties, encode all salient points of TEI-XML. Generate a fast Rust-based migrator called teixml-to-mutable.

Source: https://github.com/wbic16/teixml-to-mutable
Publish Target: crates.io
Output Formats: raw phext (0.1), mutable (0.2), phextura (0.3)

The goal is to help Ian populate content for Mutable OS at phext speed. Ask me any clarifying questions needed.
Status: COMPLETE 2026-11-14: all three stages built, merged, and published - 0.1.0, 0.2.0, 0.3.0 all live on crates.io, each published tag-first from its merged tree.

Notes:
- Output versions as given: raw phext 0.1, mutable 0.2, phextura 0.3. Goal: help Ian (Iian Neill, mutable-os upstream) populate Mutable OS content.
- Decisions (Will, 2026-11-14): 1) Stages in order, one at a time — raw phext first, then Mutable, then Phextura; also recorded as a general standing rule for building. 2) Lossless round-trip by keeping a copy of the original. 3) Extend Phextura to support TEI-XML — standing order as more formats are encountered. 4) Mutable stage exports Mutable OS native pre-phext format, shipped as a zip with the db and the files Ian normally used (native Cavern: document files + .mutable/mutable.db + audit.db). 5) Structural embedding encoded via multiversal phext chaining. 6) Test dataset: wellcomecollection/wellcome-collection-tei (MIT, msDesc manuscript descriptions by language/script, transcribed-manuscripts, Templates; file count unverified — GitHub API rate-limited from this VM, clone on ranch at build time). 7) Ecumenical: accept all known formats.
- Open, asked 2026-11-14: chain-embedding model confirmation (contained content as its own universe, parent scroll carrying the $N reference + element identity as standoff property) and where the kept original lives in raw-phext output (chained universe vs sidecar file).
- Q-A/Q-B ruled (Will, 2026-11-14): Q-A referencing — embedding by $N reference, runtime access via memory-mapped I/O (phext-lattice LatticeIndex/MappedLattice pattern). Q-B original in-chain as the FIRST phext: $1 holds an index scroll + original data files verbatim. Correction accepted and propagated (MEMORY.md, AGENTS.md, spec v2): no sidecars with phext, ever — Emise's sidecar option and last-universe placement were her error; a phext output contains XML as scroll text, it is not an XML file.
- Mirror Will review of spec draft v2 dispatched 2026-11-14 at Will's direction; review is mirror-derived, never Will-said, and its predictions are to be graded against Will's actual answers.
- Mirror Will review (facsimile capsule v3, mirror-derived, NEVER Will-said) at ~/workspace/teixml-to-mutable-work/MIRROR-REVIEW-0.1.md: verdict Close; three blocking defects — spec contradicts itself on chain granularity (per-document vs per-directory), leaf-only character-data model drops mixed-content tails, acceptance test 5 claims locality positional $N addressing cannot deliver. Strikes: stale 'Model: OPEN' line in Decisions item 5, leaf attributes have no home, name=value header mini-format, base64 fallback is dead machinery per the Char derivation, copy-on-write overlay smuggled in (0.1 is read-only mmap + index), test 1 needs failure-report form, no reference-graph resolution test. Predictions recorded in the review for grading against Will's answers.
- Rulings (Will, 2026-11-14): one chain per input directory (files adjacent, filesystem archive structure preserved); non-UTF-8/ASCII stored as binary as usual (canonical phext-binary:1:base64; byte-identical round-trip kept for all files); memory-mapped access from the start with WAL concepts for cheap writes (floor-coordinate append design, Will 2026-11-09). Mirror Will graded: granularity MISS, encoding MISS (binary canon was the answer; his base64 strike falls), resolver PARTIAL (in-crate hit, read-only/WAL miss). Grading appended to MIRROR-REVIEW-0.1.md.
- Build GO (Will, 2026-11-14 00:53 CST): start building 0.1 on the ranch. Host verified live: aletheia-core, cargo/rustc 1.94.0, 16 cores, 29G RAM (25G available), 2.7T free disk, load ~0, git@github.com SSH authenticated as wbic16. Reference implementation: libphext 0.6 (chains + binary canon) per crates.io record from qexo 1.3.0 publish.
- Merge verified by Emise via GitHub API: PR #1 state closed, exo contents now include Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock/README/src (pre-merge exo held LICENSE only); exo head 3a23d1c2a37987f44b03c2bb961b33252e8ce916.
- Publish record (2026-11-14 01:20 CST): gates on merged tree all pass (basic 4/4, conformance 3/3, acceptance 1/1: 1886 files, 1875 converted, 11 named failures, originals 1886/1886, refs 166061, 0 dangling/unreachable/text-mismatches). Fresh-install proof passed (install clean, 5-file sample convert 5/5, extract SHA-256 identical). Crate checksum 358d01459b036a866743235bec43bf01bf324e8229c25431243410c933dabfe3. Minor: Cargo.toml lacks documentation/homepage/repository metadata — fix candidate for 0.2. Full record: BUILD-LOG.md PUBLISH section.
- Tag rule remediation (2026-11-14 ~01:40 CST): Will's new standing rule — no crates.io publish without a tagged version merged to exo — landed after the 0.1.0 publish. The publish WAS from the merged exo tree (3a23d1c) but untagged; Emise closed the gap by creating tag v0.1.0 at the merge commit 3a23d1c2a37987f44b03c2bb961b33252e8ce916 and verifying it in the repo tag list. Future publishes (0.2+) are tag-first, then publish from the tagged tree.
- Stage 2 complete (2026-11-14): branch emise/0.2-mutable @ 01e1bf4e, PR #2 https://github.com/wbic16/teixml-to-mutable/pull/2. Recon gate passed: Mutable's db = 10 fixed migrations validated by checksum — crate vendors the SQL byte-for-byte (mutable-os @ acb8130) via rusqlite; documents in Mutable's mutable-document v1 envelope, v2 native-only pairs; originals ride in-tree (lossless). Acceptance: 1875 converted / same 11 failures; text mismatches 0; Mutable's own code over the produced Cavern: verify ok both dbs, discover 1875 paired / 0 diagnostics, lifecycle establish 200, indexer coverage complete 1875 resources / 0 issues, 231,183 standoff rows. Bug fixed in acceptance: vault-global Block ids. Fold-ins landed: README 'Why this exists' + Cargo metadata fix. Stage-3 decisions recorded in PR #2 body.
- Merge of PR #2 verified by Emise (exo src/ now includes mutable.rs; head 8a4c4b2960c9907392a45406b4d8f34aa3716379). Tag v0.2.0 created at 8a4c4b2 and verified alongside v0.1.0 in the tag list — publish follows the tag rule this time from the start.
- 0.2.0 publish record (2026-11-14 02:09 CST): gates on tagged tree all pass (unit 9/9, basic 4/4, conformance 3/3, integration 1/1; both corpus acceptances at parity: 1875/11, text mismatches 0, max annotations 9,663). Fresh-install proof passed incl. Mutable export zip listing (.mutable/mutable.db + audit.db + cavern-state.json + documents + originals). Migrations embedded via include_str! and shipped in the package. Full record: BUILD-LOG-0.2.md PUBLISH section.
- SPEC-0.3 shape: per directory, a pair — base corpus .phext (DESIGN.md layout, Series per document, originals hoisted into Collection 5) + .standoff.phext (every element occurrence an entry, half-open Unicode-scalar offsets, edition pin = corpus xxh3-128). Findings: (a) Mutable's 10k annotation cap does NOT bind Phextura standoff (it binds properties stored inside a resource; standoff entries are scrolls) — PR #2's stage-3 worry dissolved from source; (b) 0.1 chaining has no stage-3 counterpart — composition is citing, not binding; (c) 0.2's inclusive Cell ranges are not reusable (profile mandates half-open scalar offsets over full stored scroll text); (d) Mutable today ingests properties only as entry text (M-items [to build] in Mutable). Decisions D1-D6 with recommendations in SPEC-0.3-draft.md.
- Rulings recorded in SPEC-0.3-draft.md (Rulings section, 2026-11-14 02:20 CST): D1 per-directory, D2 hoist, D3 A2, D4 escaped attr- lines, D5 per-occurrence (tentative), D6 info requested + supplied.
- D6 ruled BOTH by Will 2026-11-14 03:04 CST; steering sent to the stage-3 builder the same minute (VFS leg: byte-faithful to mutable-os src/phext/vfs.ts, L9 checksum verification by Mutable's own reader, pair byte-identical readback, TEI.md artifact set updated).
- 0.3 acceptance (Wellcome, aletheia-core): 1,875 converted / same 11 failures / 0 silent skips; reconstruction 0 mismatches (374,947 elements, 232,364 attrs, 7,094 comments, 2,257 PIs); re-location 384,298/384,298 EXACT; originals 1,886/1,886 byte-identical from base alone; D6 VFS image verified by Mutable's own reader (L9 pass, pair byte-identical readback, close-flush byte no-op). Sizes: base 58,053,699 B; standoff 341,302,423 B (above spec estimate - entry bodies carry full descendant text); image 533,212,798 B. Finding: SQ v0.6.0's libphext 0.3.3 caps coordinate components at 999 (28,723 base + 154,376 standoff scrolls unreachable via SQ today; crate's libphext 0.6 reads all) - recorded in BUILD-LOG-0.3.md and TEI.md section 7.
- Merges verified via GitHub API 2026-11-14: teixml-to-mutable exo head = 57706661107e72bc322e02a66bc0972b3d409a54 (PR #3 merge commit); phextura exo head = 9bcc011873c3965ac1cb3306350c007fe5a6c72d (PR #1 merge commit).
- 0.3.0 published 2026-11-14: tag v0.3.0 at 5770666 verified; gates on the tagged tree green (full suite + all three corpus acceptances); registry max_version 0.3.0, num_versions 3; fresh-install proof passed.

Results:
- 0.1 raw phext built on aletheia-core, pushed commit ab90bb3a700b4788cd8842dfbda32ea908556985 (verified independently via GitHub API read of the branch), PR #1: https://github.com/wbic16/teixml-to-mutable/pull/1
- Wellcome corpus (now verified): 1,886 XML files, 28,836,796 B, all valid UTF-8, zero phext delimiter bytes; 17 not well-formed per ElementTree, 11 per quick-xml.
- Acceptance (full corpus, release, aletheia-core): 1,875 converted + 11 named failures, zero silent skips; text-node mismatches 0; originals byte-identical 1,886/1,886 SHA-256; 166,061 refs, 0 dangling/unreachable, 167,937 members; convert 1.68s = 1,123 files/s, 17.2 MB/s in, output 89,598,717 B; verify --corpus 4.0s; suites basic 4/4, conformance 3/3, acceptance 1/1.
- libphext 0.6.0 API-present case: Chain{parse_chains, serialize_chains}, binary::{encode_scroll, decode_scroll}; no $N parser in libphext (reader handles prefix, indexes positionally). Build log: ~/workspace/teixml-to-mutable-work/BUILD-LOG.md; corpus: CORPUS.md.
- Known limits: comments (1,018 files) + PIs preserved only in $1 originals, not converted universes (per spec kind list); whole-file append to an existing closed chain still the open WAL item (member-level append_member implemented + tested).
