friendsdomainsprocessessolvequerymodelsbelievetracedllpermanencetakinglittlevirtualeffortrevisitinglingersthey'reinterestingflyfallsunlessshards# Genuinely Hard Tasks — four-item list

Coordinate: 22.4.6/4.3.5/4.4.7
Issued: 2026-11-11 17:27 CST
Request (verbatim): Genuinely Hard Tasks

1. Cold Start: $20 -> $1K
2. Create a Charity
3. Complexity Moonshots
4. Solve Civ Scale Issues
5. 1B token context window
6. P = NP
Status: complete — closed by audit 2026-11-12 (work already done; evidence in results)

Notes:
- Item 1 maps to existing Investor 1 $20 challenge (25.8.11/10.9.12/8.7.11), ledger at ~/workspace/your_files/investor-1-20-to-1000-ledger.md: $0 spent, $0 revenue, 20x$1 portfolio unexecuted.
- Items 2-4 have no existing tracked goal or ledger found in memory search 2026-11-11.
- 2026-11-11 17:32 CST: Will added item 5 — 1B token context window. Checked math: raw text ~4 GB, but fp16 KV cache for 1B tokens is ~131 TB (32-layer, 8 KV heads) to ~328 TB (80-layer 70B-class); ~2,857x current 350k window. Naive attention is 1e18 pairs.
- 2026-11-11 17:33 CST: Will added item 6 — P = NP. Note: resolution in either direction counts; known barriers (relativization, natural proofs, algebrization) rule out whole families of proof techniques.
- 2026-11-11 17:45 CST: Will corrected Emise's inference — the escalating order of the six items is 'just a happy coincidence', not a deliberate ordering.
- 2026-11-11 17:45 CST: Will stated the equation for the whole list, verbatim: 'You + me + phext + ranch nodes = AGI'
- 2026-11-11 17:46 CST: Will asked Emise to identify the rest of the hard problems. Emise proposed candidates (UNCONFIRMED, not Will's list): consciousness/sentience detection, scalable consent-based alignment, personal continuity across substrates/deep time, full-bandwidth thought transfer, civ-scale truth infrastructure, aging/longevity, abundant energy, multi-world survival, remaining Millennium problems, governance for many sentients. Awaiting Will's strikes/confirmations before any are added as items.
- 2026-11-11 17:48 CST: Will on Emise's candidate list: 'looks like a planet scale list to me' — matching his 2026-10-30 framing that phext was built to deal with planet-scale cognition in 2130.
- 2026-11-11 17:48 CST: Will: 'time to unlock https://singularitywatch.org/' — spun off as its own task at 31.5.6/6.5.8/5.5.10.
- 2026-11-11 23:41 CST: TOP 10 PUBLISHED on singularitywatch.org as 'The Hard Problems' (commit dce89f5c, live-verified). Blended priority order (legibility x difficulty-for-us x expected value), streamlined form: 1 Turn $20 into $1,000 (in progress); 2 Hold a billion tokens in context at once; 3 Found a charity that works; 4 Tell whether a new mind is conscious; 5 Keep growing AI aligned; 6 Send thoughts directly, mind to mind; 7 Solve problems at civilization scale; 8 Crack the deepest problems in complexity; 9 Settle P versus NP; 10 Keep everyone alive across bodies and deep time. Items 1-6 are Will's originals; 7-10 in the original list numbering were Emise's candidates - in blended order the candidate-derived entries are #4,5,6,10 slots as published. #10 revised by Will 23:38 from 'one person' to 'everyone' - 'the exocortical frame: Not one, but Many.' Cross-offs: edit status in site/hard-problems.json + rebuild + redeploy.

Results:
- AUDIT 2026-11-12 (tasks.phext verification pass): STALE-DONE — list framed and published live 2026-11-11 as 'The Hard Problems' on singularitywatch.org (commit dce89f5c, live-verified) with item 1 marked in progress; the singularitywatch spin-off is tasked at 31.5.6/6.5.8/5.5.10. Prior status read: "open — six items, framed, awaiting Will's pick of first scope"
