Name ranch nodes by their short hostname, never by bare IP

Whenever connecting to a Tailscale address, look up its DNS name: each ranch node has a Tailscale DNS address, and the IP cross-references back to a short hostname, like Rock Mountain or aletheia-core. Always map IP to DNS name to short hostname and refer to nodes by their short names, never by bare IP.

— Given 2026-11-04 · Source: MEMORY.md · [distilled]
