let# Gamify Personal AGI in qexo: time-dilation rate + progress vs SOTA per token

Coordinate: 24.5.8/12.6.6/7.4.8
Issued: 2026-11-14 01:52 CST
Request (from session record): Will (2026-11-14 01:52-01:53 CST): 'qexo needs to gamify Personal AGI — I want to know what my current time dilation rate is, based upon effort in the past week' + 'also rate our progress relative to SOTA per token' + 'assume that tokens and cash will flow once we achieve efficiency supremacy.' This is the game layer over qexo bench (53.14.8/18.8.27/6.9.10): the MOAT-style bars become a Personal AGI HUD — headline metric TIME DILATION RATE = baseline-equivalent output produced per unit of Will's effort over a trailing 7-day window; second headline = PROGRESS vs SOTA PER TOKEN on the shared benchmark set (verified progress divided by tokens spent, ours vs the funded setups'), with per-watt alongside. Planning assumption, recorded as Will's premise: tokens and cash are DOWNSTREAM — they flow once efficiency supremacy is achieved, so the game optimizes efficiency (progress per token / per watt / per Will-hour) rather than resource acquisition.
Status: recorded — presentation layer over the bench task; token accounting instrumentation is the gating measurement

Notes:
- Current rates from the record (DIAGNOSIS.md §1.2-1.5, measured 2026-11-07, reaffirmed in the 2026-11-14 Cold Start diagnosis): effort-normalized time dilation = 80-120x (working range 1,000-1,500 code LOC per Will active hour vs Will's baseline of 100 LOC/day/developer = ~80-120 developer-equivalents); conservative measured floor 1,113 LOC/active hr; calendar/research dilation in Will's own framing = ~50 years per year (~1 year of 2025-baseline research output per week). The bench must show the range as a bar, not a fake point value.
- SOTA-per-token is NOT yet a measured number: token spend per verified outcome is not instrumented across substrates (DIAGNOSIS §3.3/§4.1 — reset cliffs are calendared, the loop itself is unmeasured). First bench job: log tokens per task/benchmark so the ratio becomes real; until then the SOTA-per-token bar renders as a target with current = unmeasured, never as an invented score.
