- Will's direction (2026-11-09 21:57 CST, Architecture thread): 'make sure all tcc commands are rewritten to phcc.' Executed as PATCHES F51 in wbic16/phcc on aletheia-core (~/phcc-rename/tree), base = published tip 8217e426. Census first: every surface where a user runs `tcc ...` or meets the command name `tcc` as this compiler — rewritten or deliberately kept with reason, all recorded in the PATCHES F51 entry.
- Binary mechanics: Makefile PROGS builds phcc$(EXESUF) from the same tcc.o; cross compilers are <target>-phcc (arm64-phcc, i386-phcc, x86_64-win32-phcc); TCC_LOCAL (native + test-install forms) names phcc so the whole test suite follows with no test edits; libtcc1.a prerequisite, %-libtcc1.a rule, XTCC and libtcc.def prerequisite name phcc; phcc_p/phcc_c/phcc_s variants; install BINCHECK + install-unx globs ship phcc + *-phcc; clean removes the new names. Target selection verified compile-time (per-target DEF-* defines), never argv[0]-based, so the rename cannot mis-select a backend.
- Install layout: configure's default runtime dir is ${libdir}/phcc (Windows default prefix C:/Program Files/phcc), summary line reads 'phcc directory'; tcc.h CONFIG_TCCDIR fallback is /usr/local/lib/phcc. Scratch-prefix install verified: bin/phcc + lib/phcc runtime, installed binary compiles and runs with no -B.
- Strings: tcc.c usage/-run/-hh/-B/-ar/-impdef/-E -dM help + 'phcc version' banner; tcctools.c -ar/-impdef usage+errors, -m message, could-not-run message, and the tcc_tool_cross sibling re-exec suffix '-tcc' -> '-phcc' (the one place the name is machinery: phcc -m32 defers to i386-phcc); libtcc.c location-less diagnostic prefix 'phcc:' + memory-full message; tccdbg.c DWARF producer 'phcc ' + version. Docs/examples: README quickstart, docs/BUILDING.md, verify_examples.sh, example READMEs, hello.c comments + shebang, multifile Makefile, ex1.c/ex4.c shebangs, phext/README.md + phext/tests/Makefile dogfood lines, .gitignore binary patterns.
- The one internal invocation the census grep missed: lib/Makefile's TCC/XTCC named $(TOP)/$(X)tcc$(EXESUF) (the just-built compiler that builds libtcc1.a) — hidden by the 'libtcc' filter substring; the first renamed build caught it (GNU make's builtin rule tried to link a target named 'tcc'); fixed and recorded in PATCHES F51 as the census method's measured limit.
- Kept deliberately (reasons in PATCHES F51): the libtcc API names (libtcc.h, tcc_new, libtcc.a/.so, libtcc1.a, tcclib.h, tccdefs.h); source file names and object stems; build-system identifiers and the --tccdir/--tcc-switches option spellings (defaults/prose updated); the conftest.c/CC_NAME compiler-identity probe pair (__TINYC__ token other build systems detect); upstream's own material (root README, Changelog, tcc-doc.texi + generated tcc.1/html/info, win32/ tree, .github/workflows, slurp.sh, attribution lines, tar target's upstream tarball names); historical records (BENCHMARKS.md, earlier PATCHES prose, PARITY.md receipts, Library-10000 listings, tools/build_reissue.py, tools/phcc_gate.py's 'tcc:' verdict label — gate receipt format; relabelling would break the refresh fixed-point property). NO compatibility shim anywhere: build/install/scripts produce only phcc (+ <target>-phcc); the single name-dependent machinery was renamed with the binary.
- Diff: 23 files, +107/-107, every change a name substitution in place (PATCHES.md excluded; it gained the F51 entry, 4 amended + 4 new delta rows). Newly divergent vs upstream at F51: configure, tcctools.c, lib/Makefile, examples/ex1.c, examples/ex4.c (all upstream-identical before F51 — verified by diff vs rebase base c638ddfb).
- Publish coordination: while this ran, the upstream-seal stack published as a3b1a8e6 on 8217e426 (upstream.phext.xz + UPSTREAM.md + tools/upstream_carry.py; that commit deliberately did not touch phcc.phext). This F51 stack is based on 8217e426 and needs the standard publish rebase onto a3b1a8e6. Its refresh ran on a tree without the seal files, so after the rebase the phext does not yet carry UPSTREAM.md/tools/upstream_carry.py — the documented precedent position (cf. phcc_harvest.py between the D9 publish and its sweep); the next standing refresh sweeps them in.
- Node/thermal: aletheia-core, Tctl 34.4 C at start; all builds serial; no thermal events. Local commits authored as Emise <emise@mirrorborn>.

Results:
- LOCAL stack on 8217e426 (ranch ~/phcc-rename/tree, NOT pushed — coordinator publishes): acd1751c 'F51: the command surface is phcc' (23 files renamed + PATCHES.md F51 entry) -> bfec0ab6 'phext refresh: F51' (phcc.phext 65,085,973 B SHA-256 0945b10f206cb3a3356d9a298e9336248460aba3374c4c90dcfdb2cf6e4b3a10, 64,399 scrolls; seal 1bf02c1707ea673202a83ba6f2ca1f7f8b1e6153a4b1a474a35f872b6509b902). Publish needs rebase onto a3b1a8e6 (the seal commit that landed meanwhile).
- Regression net on the renamed tree (aletheia-core): clean configure+make produces phcc and no tcc; banner 'phcc version 1.0.0 2026-11-09 main@8217e426* (x86_64 Linux)'; make cross-arm64/cross-i386 produce arm64-phcc/i386-phcc (arm64 object verified AArch64 ELF); make test ALL TESTS PASSED; examples/verify_examples.sh 19 passed / 0 failed / 0 skipped under phcc, gcc 13.3.0 and clang 18.1.3; conformance spot 332/333, diverge set exactly [a_pp_018], 0 unclassified (path+name-corrected runner copy; results record the phcc banner); static gate cells 3/3 (hello runs; repaired IRELATIVE check passes with .rela.plt [0x404510, +0x228) — the D9 range exactly; Lua byte-identical static vs dynamic; static phccbox smoke byte-identical, awk 42); phccbox build spot: gzip 1.14 bundle configured+built with CC='<tree>/phcc -B<tree>' per the box's phase-2 recipe, round-trip verified.
- Decision-rule receipt: fresh clone -> README quickstart builds and runs phcc end-to-end (in-tree -run and -o forms, and the scratch-prefix installed binary with no -B) without the name tcc ever being typed. -m32 deferral: renamed phcc finds i386-phcc, re-executes it and proceeds to real compilation, stopping only at the host's missing 32-bit system crt files; the pre-rename D10 tree in the same setup cannot find its sibling at all ('tcc: could not run ./i386-tcc').
- Refresh receipts: baseline gate fixed-point OK and baseline reseal OK on the published F49+F50 phext (1e06260a); gate run twice on the new phext — byte-identical verdicts (GATE-REPRODUCIBLE-OK); seal/unseal round-trip byte-identical; unpack --from vol2 613/613 and --from vol3 613/613, every file SHA-256-verified; scroll census vs base: 1,631 changed, 0 added, 0 removed (PATCHES.md + the 23 renamed files' Source/member/Design scrolls + manifests + register + verdict).
- PUBLISHED 2026-11-09 (coordinator publish pass): remote verified main == exo == a3b1a8e6 immediately before the rebase (fresh fetch). The two-commit local stack (acd1751c F51 rename, bfec0ab6 refresh, on 8217e426) rebased CLEANLY onto a3b1a8e6 — no phext conflict, the refresh commit applied as-is (no regeneration needed) as 76507c5c (F51) + 6ca3eab1 (refresh); the carried phext is byte-identical to the rename agent's refresh (phcc.phext sha256 0945b10f206cb3a3356d9a298e9336248460aba3374c4c90dcfdb2cf6e4b3a10), and per the standing precedent the upstream seal's two text files (UPSTREAM.md, tools/upstream_carry.py) enter the carry at the next standing refresh. Post-rebase verification on aletheia-core (Tctl 34-36 C throughout): gate baseline fixed-point PASS (gate re-run reproduces the carried phext byte-identically, verdict sha256 60ce8b46...); fresh git-archive build: configure+make rc 0, binary named phcc (529,208 B), NO tcc binary, banner 'phcc version 1.0.0 (x86_64 Linux)'; make test ALL TESTS PASSED; unpack 613/613 via vol2 AND 613/613 via vol3 (348 segments + 265 bridge), trees content-identical except the manifest route label; README quickstart spot-run: -run and compiled hello both print 'Hello, world!'. Push: exo first (a3b1a8e6..6ca3eab1), main fast-forwarded to the same commit, NO force; ls-remote confirms both branches at 6ca3eab1d2bd2fb0b8716e5fc069d68a91d31d78 (GitHub's GH001 large-file advisory for phcc.phext noted, standing). Fresh-clone verification at the published tip: HEAD 6ca3eab1, phcc.phext sha256 0945b10f... matches the published refresh, seal sha256 1bf02c17...; clean build yields phcc only (banner carries the commit: 'phcc version 1.0.0 2026-11-09 main@6ca3eab'), quickstart compiles and runs rc 0. One process note: the first fresh-clone script's heredoc expanded its $-expressions at write time, baking rc=128 strings into its log — the underlying clone/build/run outputs were genuine, and every check was re-run directly with clean receipts before this record was written.
