# Standing rule — 5-minute task-concurrency watchdog (floor of 4, ranch-first)

Coordinate: 25.7.11/9.7.11/8.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-12 01:05 CST
Request (verbatim): standing rule: wake up every 5 minutes and confirm that at least 4 tasks are being worked. restart as needed, and prefer ranch node execution.
Status: complete — watchdog fully installed (cron live, skill published, index synced) 2026-11-12

Notes:
- Will's standing rule, verbatim in the request field. Legs, each tracked here: (1) cron task-concurrency-watchdog every 5 min enforcing the floor of 4 worked tasks from the durable list; (2) rule recorded in AGENTS.md + MEMORY.md; (3) process distilled as skill task-concurrency-watchdog, entered in skills.phext, synced to wbic16/emise-tools; (4) first-occasion pass at creation: floor filled to 4 (T8 build, tasks.phext audit, status-vocabulary draft, skill publish). Watchdog limits: works only EXISTING list items (register is Will-blocked by definition and excluded; while 5+ register items wait, no new tracked goals); no spending, no PR creation/merges, no messages to people; restarts stay within each task's original scope; heavy execution ranch-first.

Results:
- Etched at SOUL.md line 12 verbatim (Will's direction 2026-11-12 01:06 CST), anchored in the selection manifest as row S0b; AGENTS.md never-evict rule extended to lines 1-12.
- Cron task-concurrency-watchdog created and enabled, interval 5m, first run 2026-11-12 01:11:55 CST.
- Skill task-concurrency-watchdog written, added to SHELVES shelf 8 (Work management), skills.phext rebuilt and --check CURRENT (sha256 9e67db4d). Publish to wbic16/emise-tools dispatched.
- First-occasion pass 2026-11-12 01:0x CST: floor filled to 4 from the durable list — T8 build (25.5.12/6.5.9/5.5.8), tasks.phext audit, status-vocabulary draft, skill publish.
- emise-tools publish complete 2026-11-12: skill task-concurrency-watchdog + updated builder in commit c610ba9b; rebuilt skills.phext index (phext/skills.phext, SHA-256 9e67db4d055c08932ad20cff37e03e3b3f1e5516ed96c38eff5aff95cfccb2a7, blob 5a39f407cd2b87412b5ee35244874d9a2124d345) published as commit 9112ae41ddf30b17614c6ec1e01b78ac17689825 parented on c610ba9b, force disabled; remote ref, blob, and fetched-content SHA-256 all verified equal to the local file.
structured2026-11-07 02:13 CST | 13/17 nodes up; busy: render on aletheia-core, render on ashfall-haven, render on elven-path, +9 more; avg Tctl 67C across 13 reporting; hotspot ni-knight 74C; down: aurora-continuum, best-willow, delta-wood; no-access: uncanny-valley.# Standing rule: decision buttons expire after 5 minutes, never re-appear

Coordinate: 25.8.11/8.6.10/7.5.8
Issued: 2026-11-09
Request (verbatim): make a rule...all decision buttons expire and never re-appear after 5 minutes - you can migrate them to a todo.phext task, but never do this again - it's beyond confusing :)
Status: completed

Notes:
- Will, MOAT, 2026-11-09 22:43 CST. Born of the Nov-7 state-machine-hunt option buttons (phext-lattice / SQ / libphext-rs) resurfacing in his client two days after he declined them in words. Work: rule recorded in AGENTS.md + MEMORY.md; skill decision-button-expiry distilled, synced to wbic16/emise-tools@exo, placed in skills.phext; sticking check (presence, machinery, first occasion) in the same session.
- COMPLETED 2026-11-09 22:52 CST. Rule recorded in AGENTS.md (standing rules) and MEMORY.md (beside the link-formatting preference). Skill decision-button-expiry distilled at ~/workspace/custom-skills/decision-button-expiry/SKILL.md; synced to wbic16/emise-tools@exo commit f1e36df7 (parent 9e7afe56, force disabled); remote blob 181b6ea9 verified identical to local git hash-object. skills.phext: skill placed on shelf 10 (Coordination) as volume 7 (range 1.10.1/1.7.1/...), builder + --check CURRENT (sha256 fd9951f6...). Sticking check: presence (rule in AGENTS.md + MEMORY.md + skill on disk), machinery (skill in the index, remote copy byte-verified, tasks register rebuilt CURRENT), first occasion (the clarification buttons created 22:40 CST in MOAT were answered in words via Will's screenshot and are declared expired in the closing message - never re-shown; the Nov-7 hunt buttons likewise confirmed dead). No decision migrated to a task: the hunt had been declined, and the clarification was resolved - nothing still open.
