# Draft Product Hunt 'Connect with Investors' answers (competitors, revenue/growth, anything else)

Coordinate: 25.9.11/12.8.15/7.8.9
Issued: 2026-11-09 20:21 CST
Request (from session record): Product Hunt info - help me fill out these questions: Who are your competitors, and what do you understand about this idea that they don't? What's your revenue and/or growth rate? Anything else you would like investors to know?
Status: complete — drafts delivered; Singular check clean; answer 3 opening corrected for the UNL degree

Notes:
- Form is Product Hunt's Connect with Investors (never shared publicly). Will's two existing answers shown in his screenshot: founder = 'I am building the Exocortex of 2130, one scroll at a time.'; idea = files/directories designed for 1 MHz/64 KB, today 5 GB/s disks but no way to handle an ecosystem of files. Honesty constraint on the revenue answer: Phext Edit is free/open source, pre-revenue; growth stated in verifiable build terms, no invented metrics.
- Correction (Will, 2026-11-09 20:24 CST): he holds a BS in Computer Science from UNL (Dec 2006) — verified on his canonical resume. Answer (3)'s 'no pedigree — self-taught, Nebraska' line is wrong as drafted; corrected rewrite proposed to Will: keep the receipts-over-resume point, state the degree plainly, frame pedigree as elite-brand channels. USER.md + dated note corrected.

Results:
- Singular verification (2026-11-09): all three answers as drafted pass the checker clean against the combined 41,302-word archive list (zero exceptions — every load-bearing name incl. Notion/Obsidian/Roam/Rust/Neovim/SaaS/MCP is in the archive; digits are not tokenized). Answer 3's opening was replaced after Will's education correction with a Singular-clean sentence carrying the full facts: 'I have 30+ years of shipping software. BS in Computer Science, University of Nebraska–Lincoln, 2006 — a real degree and no brand-name pedigree, which in practice means my work gets judged by artifacts or not at all.' (36 words, clean; whole file 401 words clean.) Final text: ~/workspace/singular-ph-answers/singular-answers.md.
atBurn perishable substrate capacity before its reset; a context reservoir is never a burn target

Steer work across substrates by value density and reset cliff: Claude's capacity is the main perishable one (resets Wednesday), Grok's a smaller Thursday cliff kept for Grok Bots, Muse free capacity expires Fridays, ChatGPT is a context reservoir that is never a burn-down target, and the unmetered local shell absorbs always-on and background work.

