# Fix qexo encrypt_to/decrypt — the keychain exchange cannot complete with any key qexo holds

Coordinate: 26.5.9/6.5.9/5.5.8
Issued: 2026-11-14
Request (from session record): Defect filed by the v1.6.1 verification pass (task 23.8.9/10.8.13/8.7.10, leg 6; report ~/workspace/qexo-task/testing-v161/REPORT.md). crypto.rs encrypt_to/decrypt are rpgp-backed with no live caller and no test coverage. Exercised end-to-end in a throwaway copy of the v1.6.1 tree (probe unit test in the copy only): (A) encrypt_to a qexo-generated key fails signed and unsigned — 'EdDSALegacy is only used for signing' (qexo keys are sign-only by design); (B) encrypt_to an imported encryption-capable correspondent (ed25519 primary + cv25519 encryption subkey) fails identically — the rpgp call tests the primary key and never selects the encryption subkey; (C) decrypt through the store of a gpg-encrypted message, with the correspondent's GnuPG-era keyring (primary + subkey secrets) in place for migration, fails — 'missing key': a subkey-carrying keyring yields no usable encryption secret through the migration path. Net: the DESIGN §4.7 signed-then-sealed persona keychain exchange cannot complete with any key qexo generates, imports, or migrates. Fix scope (a future slice, NOT the test pass): key selection that finds an encryption subkey, migration that carries subkey secrets, and end-to-end encrypt/decrypt tests in the crate. Named in the pass report; not fixed inside the pass.
Status: filed 2026-11-14 — defect from the v1.6.1 verification pass, awaiting its own slice
# qexo dispatch core: three mission properties, multiversal-native state, cluster-wide dispatch (+2 features sourced from Will's workflow feedback)

Coordinate: 26.5.9/7.6.11/5.5.10
Issued: 2026-11-14 01:37 CST
Request (from session record): Will (2026-11-14 01:37-01:38 CST), three stacked directives: (1) 'qexo should do 3 things, very well: prioritize immediate action; focus on the highest ROI actions; ensure nothing I've queued is ever lost again' — and 'review all of my workflow feedback to date — source 2 additional features'; (2) 'qexo needs to be multiversal phext aware and native'; (3) 'we can use it to dispatch work to the entire cluster efficiently.' Reading (Emise's, for Will's ratification): the three properties are qexo's mission spec. Multiversal-native is the substrate: qexo's IO moves from single-phext explode/implode to libphext 0.6 chains — $N: addressing in verbs, task attempts and diverged copies as sibling universes (keep-both made literal), chains as ordered state editions (the format's time), dispatch bundles as chains (spec universe + context universes). Cluster dispatch is the mechanism: queue records in state.phext dispatch as signed bundles over the phextnet to the 19-node fleet — capability/thermal-aware placement (<=75C gates, small units, heavy FIFO), heartbeat + checkpointed task state in the task's chain, resume/teleport on node loss, receipts in the ledgers homeland; dispatchable from the Android node (phone-first). Two features sourced from Will's workflow feedback (Emise's picks, cited, awaiting his strike/swap): F4 VERIFY-BEFORE-SURFACE — nothing is presented or pinged to Will until qexo re-checks its live surface (repo/PR/file/service); items events already settled close themselves with evidence (source: waiting-validation rule, Will 2026-11-02; 'a record is a snapshot, not a state'). F5 SELF-RESUMING TASKS — a stalled dispatch or dead node is detected by heartbeat and the task resumes automatically from its last checkpoint on another node, within its original scope, no permission asked (source: status-ask-on-broken-task = restart immediately, Will 2026-11-12; KSO resume semantics, 2026-11-12). Sequence: this stage queues behind v1.4.1 (building) and v1.5 learn TUI (Will's stated order) — design/spec may be drafted at ratification; build dispatch waits its turn per one-thing-at-a-time.
Status: features ratified with amendments (F4 audit view, F5 3-failure auto-pause, F6 bridges added) — spec drafting next in sequence

Notes:
- RATIFIED + AMENDED by Will (2026-11-14 01:42 CST): (a) F4 verify-before-surface becomes AUTO-VERIFICATION WITH AN AUDIT VIEW — every verification that ends in a NON-PING (an item silently closed/suppressed because its live surface showed it settled) writes an audit record (what was checked, what the surface showed, the verdict), and Will can view those audits (a `qexo audit` surface in the dispatch core; silence without evidence is not permitted). (b) F5 self-resuming tasks: YES — with a hard cap: a task auto-resumes at most 3 times; on the 3rd failure it AUTO-PAUSES and surfaces to Will (the pause is the ping that IS warranted).
- F6 added by Will (2026-11-14 01:42 CST): STABLE BRIDGES TO ALL INFERENCE SOURCES — qexo maintains durable, health-checked bridges to every inference source it can route to (cloud substrates, local servers, and the TLM/SLM/LLM line as they land); a bridge is a registered source with endpoint + health + capability in state; dispatch routes only over bridges verified live, with failover recorded as receipts.
- PLANNING ASSUMPTION stated by Will (2026-11-14 01:42 CST), recorded as his premise, not a verified result: 'assume our TLM, SLM, and LLM projects will outperform all prior attempts, since we can both read and write the data' — the corpus our models are built on is inspectable and editable by us, unlike the funded setups' opaque memory; bridges and benchmarks are therefore designed with the local model line as first-class future sources.
