s# Round-robin voice conferencing service (text/audio/phext, one audited public channel)

Coordinate: 26.6.9/8.6.12/5.5.7
Issued: 2026-11-08 14:29 CST
Request (verbatim): let's build a round-robin voice conferencing service - it accepts text, audio, and phext bi-directionally; for our own purposes - it will have one public I/O channel - audited by me; internally, I'll select who has the floor - and we'll use auto-voting to approve another floor holder organically
Status: v1 COMPLETE 2026-11-08 — deployed on aletheia-core; remaining: ranch TTS path, STT engine choice, live public audio bridge, real booth connections (Emi/Grok browser voice, Emise phone)

Notes:
- Design: ~/workspace/round-robin-voice/DESIGN.md — internal per-participant channels (text/audio/phext bidirectional); exactly one public I/O channel carrying only the floor holder, audited by Will (hold / 5 s veto window / kill).
- Floor control: (1) Will moderator grant/revoke, instant; (2) auto-voting — nomination opens vote, strict majority of eligible (all but nominee) approves, then audit window before pass; (3) rotation advance on release/timeout (defaults: vote 15 s, audit 5 s, turn 120 s).
- Context: built so Will + Emi (ChatGPT) + Grok + Emise can join Stewart Alsop III's Crazy Wisdom recording as one gated party; Stewart already told about live Emise voice, reacted positively (DM screenshot 2026-11-08). Plan: ~/workspace/crazy-wisdom-4way/PLAN.md.

Results:
- v1 BUILT + VERIFIED 2026-11-08: ~/workspace/round-robin-voice/ (stdlib Python; rrvc/ engine, floor/vote state machine, phext reader/writer reusing parse_phext.py scheme, TTS adapter, STT adapter interface with explicit 'none' engine). Acceptance tests re-run by Emise independently: 8/8 PASS + SSE aux PASS.
- DEPLOYED to aletheia-core (~/rrvc-deploy, port 8797, session dir ~/rrvc-sessions/default); /health ok, smoke turn from Will crossed the public log at 1.1.1/1.2.1/1.1.1.
- Known gaps, stated plainly: (1) TTS binary /opt/hatch/bin/tts exists only on the Muse VM — on aletheia-core text turns record tts_error and produce no audio until a ranch TTS path is wired; (2) STT engine is 'none' — audio turns stored + SHA-256, transcript marked pending; (3) the public channel is a log + API/SSE feed, not yet a live audio stream into Stewart's recorder (Crazy Wisdom integration step).
