Issued: 2026-11-13 01:45 CST
Request (from session record): Found live by Will testing his laptop node (2026-11-13 01:41-01:45 CST). His state.phext (C:\var\lib\qexo\state.phext) contains: (a) the config record scroll at 9.9.9/2.1.1/1.1.1 with the field line 'release_signer:' EMPTY; (b) appended at the end of the file, after the 9.9.9/9.9.9/9.9.9 homeland anchor scroll, a delimiter stack (SOH x10, US x8, RS x8, GS x1) followed by a scroll whose whole text is 'release_signer: A4E7277FB3EB0E589604BE5B506DBE3FC209E755' — written by Phext Notepad, whose coordinate bar addressed that scroll as 9.9.9/2.1.1/1.1.1. qexo update --check still reads the signer as unset. So two phext implementations disagree about this file: either the appended scroll's true address differs between parsers (descending delimiter-stack reckoning), or duplicate-address scroll resolution differs. Diagnose from libphext's definition (the reference), reproduce synthetically, and report the mechanism before fixing. Sibling items for the same v1.2.1 slice: the hidden lattice verb 'select' errors '<coord>: The system cannot find the path specified. (os error 3)' on Will's Windows build, and there is no 'qexo config --release-signer' setter (Will hit the gap in the wild).
Status: complete — parser replaced by libphext-rs (v1.3.0, PR #16 merged) and the suspect fleet state wiped fleet-wide

Notes:
- DIAGNOSIS (2026-11-13, measured on a byte-for-byte synthetic; replica + full record in ~/workspace/qexo-task/interop/ and ~/workspace/qexo-task/libphext/BUILD-RECORD.md): the hand-rolled parser's ONE divergence from libphext was the library break — qexo 0x02 (STX), reference 0x01 (SOH); qexo read 0x01 as scroll content. The editor's append lands at 11.9.9/2.1.1/1.1.1 under SQ (libphext 0.3.3), libphext 0.5.0, and Will's Python parser alike; at 9.17.9/2.1.1/1.1.1 under qexo's parser; and it shadows the config record under NO reckoning — the refusal was correct on the file's terms. Will's ruling (01:48): libphext-rs is canonical. His decision (01:49): just use libphext-rs in qexo — diagnosis converted to the full fix slice.
- SELECT VERB SETTLED: not a platform bug — phext_file_ops took args[1] as a file path unconditionally, so the coordinate was opened as a path. Reproduced on Linux with the genuine v1.2.0 binary ("No such file or directory (os error 2)", exit 2; Windows reports the same condition as error 3). v1.3.0 gives select/get a one-argument state form; Will's exact command shape verified in the sandbox.
