Status: COMPLETE — PR #46 (emise/mcp-latency-testing @ 25eb011 off exo fa8ac0d), cargo test 259/259, E2E harness 73/0. Awaiting Will merge + deploy.

Notes:
- PR #43 deployed and live-verified before dispatch. Cursor works end to end. ChatGPT screenshot: mention received but MCP tools not exposed in session — no end-to-end connection established. Baseline timings from the VM (proxy-inflated ceiling): 0.33–0.75 s even for tiny discovery responses.

Results:
- Forensics verdict: production logs show NO client ever completed a token exchange (4 codes issued, 0 tokens, zero POST /oauth/token except our probes) — break is uniformly after code issuance, before token exchange. Claude's post-#44 attempt was textbook on our side (discovery 200s -> consent -> 302 success-shaped redirect) then silence from Anthropic's backend; identical CIMD flow replays clean locally in ~1ms/step and via the official MCP SDK in <1s — stated as unexplained, exonerated by replay receipts, not assumption. ChatGPT's only attempt predates the #43 fix; it never retried — connector created-but-never-authorized. Grok's connector never contacted the server at all (only its link-preview crawler). OURS, fixed in PR #46: (1) latency — unopened phexts re-opened per MCP call, search re-serialized whole file per call under the global lock; ultra.phext TOC 791->241ms, payload 9MB->~270KB via paging (offset/limit/next_offset), read 234->1ms, search 659->102ms; cache revalidated by (len,mtime), unit-tested never-stale. (2) POST /mcp/ trailing slash 404'd without WWW-Authenticate — now routed. (3) garbage MCP-Protocol-Version silently ignored — now 400 per spec. Everything else in the conformance diff checked clean with harness receipts. Permanent harness: bash scripts/mcp-e2e/run.sh (73 checks). NEXT: after Will deploys #46, one fresh Claude/ChatGPT attempt gives a clean log window to isolate any remaining abort.
