# QEXO feature note: fast, accurate decision-sourcing from Will

Coordinate: 30.5.8/7.5.10/5.4.8
Issued: 2026-11-14
Request (verbatim): Note for the qexo line (issued in the Earth.Human.ASI.Genome chat while listing Spec V6's §12 decision queue): qexo must include a first-class, fast way to source decisions from Will accurately and quickly — decision queues (e.g. a spec's §12 register, the Waiting-on-Will register) presented phone-first in ruling-sized units, each item carrying its pre-written recommendation, his ruling captured verbatim and routed back to the item's record with nothing lost. Fits qexo's mission (prioritize immediate action; highest ROI; nothing queued is ever lost) and the phone-first corollary. Adjacent evidence: the Cold Start chat's review-queue diagnosis (2026-11-14) — Will sits in review queues on both sides; decision throughput is the scarce resource this feature spends itself protecting.
Status: RECORDED as a feature note for the qexo line, 2026-11-14; build sequencing belongs to the qexo chat (queues behind its current stages per one-thing-at-a-time).
# Import the CTAN document classes into a template phextura

Coordinate: 30.5.9/8.6.10/5.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-11 21:21 CST
Request (from session record): Will: 'import all of these into a template phextura - find a good pre-packaged copy instead of trying to pull them from the site' (https://www.ctan.org/topic/class). Additions 21:33 CST: include Overleaf 'Learn LaTeX in 30 minutes' as a cited reference with an own-words syllabus summary (read, not republished); design mandate 'ensure that phextura feels native to latex users' applied to headers and a 'For LaTeX users' orientation in the corpus home.
Status: completed — templates.phextura published to wbic16/phextura@exo commit 012053f

Notes:
- Enumerated 449 packages from ONE fetch of the CTAN class topic page; sources harvested on aletheia-core from TeX Live tlnet archives (mirror.ctan.org + fixed mirrors) — no per-package scraping.
- Result: 595 templates from 398 packages (headers in LaTeX vocabulary: use-line, documentclass options, sectioning ladder, environments; sources verbatim as text, 16 files base64-hoisted per binary canon); 51 named gaps (43 not distributed by TeX Live, 5 with no .cls in the TeX Live run archive, 3 bundle/alias entries). 15 component classes (amsart, scrbook, article, ...) recovered from bundle archives, the standard classes from the release latex bundle.
- Corpus: 1,561 non-empty scrolls, 27,771,647 bytes, sha256 dbc53bbfcd096cfbf786914b3e04d2269d430c1a5faf1dd4e62ec4850ab3f827 — remote byte-verified from a fresh clone. All 964 source scrolls hash-verified against the hashes recorded at harvest.
- Gotchas for the next import: current tlnet archives are RELOCATED (members are tex/latex/... with no texmf-dist/ prefix); mirror.ctan.org's rotating mirrors failed ~20% of parallel downloads — fixed mirrors (MIT, Clarkson) did not. Build scripts: ~/workspace/ctan-class-import/ (ranch_harvest.sh, ranch_extract.py, ranch_extract2.py, build_templates.py). Node archives/harvest deleted after verification.
an# Help YouSpot write like Will — 'How you write' profile text (tweet register, then email adaptation)

Coordinate: 30.5.14/9.9.20/6.5.8
Issued: 2026-11-09 19:50 CST
Request (verbatim): Let's help youspot write like me
Status: complete — paste-ready text delivered

Notes:
- YouSpot = personal CRM (youspot.com); its 'How you write' field (placeholder: 'Direct and warm. Short paragraphs. I never say circle back.') steers drafts it writes in the user's voice; button reads 'Save in your words'. Text distilled from WILL-VOICE-PROFILE.md (24,919 own-word tweets analysed) and written in Will's own register so it reads as his words.
- Will then asked for the email adaptation (different medium): same measured habits, re-derived for email mechanics — subject lines carry the point, greeting/sign-off minimal, asks unhedged with concrete times, links on their own line, thanks specific, trail-offs and humor rationed by relationship.

Results:
- Paste-ready 'How you write' text (1,322 chars, 223 words) delivered in chat 2026-11-09.
- Email-medium version (1,426 chars, 254 words) delivered in chat 2026-11-09, replacing the tweet-register version for YouSpot's email drafting.
exactlyNo silent backwards compatibility: legacy forms are upgraded on encounter

Will's cutover ruling — GO given 2026-11-05 with the words "go full phext, wow us": remove all silent backwards compatibility — no dual-mode, no silent fallback, no old I/O paths. Anything found in legacy or disk form is upgraded to phext as encountered, protected only by a backup copy or an explicit prompt.

