# Make the qexo Android app useful — Learn You a qexo ported + high-payoff quick actions

Coordinate: 30.6.9/7.5.9/5.5.7
Issued: 2026-11-14 03:12 CST
Request (from session record): Will (2026-11-14 03:12 CST): 'OK, let's make the qexo android app useful - port learn you a qexo and make sure all of the high payoff actions are available to me quickly.' The v1.6.0 APK launcher has only four buttons (config / status / update --check / evolve --check) and dumps command output — a diagnostic shell, not a control surface. This stage: (1) Learn You a qexo as a real in-app card session (chapter/lesson context, due queue, reveal, again/good/easy grading, progress header) driven by the Rust learn engine — the deck and SM-2 state stay in the binary/state.phext, never reimplemented in Java; the wizard is TTY-only today, so the binary gains the smallest embeddable front-end protocol (plain-text line protocol, not JSON) and the app drives it over pipes. (2) High-payoff quick actions one tap from the home screen, per qexo's mission (immediate action, highest ROI): full Update and full Evolve (not just --check), Doctor + Repair (doctor --fix), List peers, Inventory, Status, Learn — checks remain available but demoted below the actions that DO things. Build in wbic16/qexo (the Android home); the protocol is shared code, so a quarterexo twin is owed under the sync rule (29.6.7/6.5.7/6.5.8) — it queues behind quarterexo PR #22 and is tracked there. Trial APK built from the Android PR branch so Will can use it immediately, signed with the SAME debug cert as the shipped v1.6.0 APK so it installs over it without wiping the node's state.
Status: complete 2026-11-14 — PR #3 merged; final release APK (versionCode 4) delivered, supersedes the trial build

Notes:
- 2026-11-14: the quarterexo twin of the --app protocol is delivered as quarterexo PR #24 (https://github.com/wbic16/quarterexo/pull/24, register #110) — the sync debt named at this task's delivery is resolved-by-delivery and discharges on Will's merge; quarterexo reaches v1.6.1 with the shared files byte-identical across both repos.

Results:
- Part 1 shipped in wbic16/qexo PR #3 (branch emise/android-learn-app-v1.6.1 @ af48ebcf, parented on exo ce0731d7; remote tree verified 44/44 blobs, delta = the 9 intended files): `qexo learn --app`, a plain-text line protocol (status/chapters/lesson/next/practice/reveal/grade/quit; key: value blocks closed by end: <command>) driving the wizard's own state machine — deck, chapter map, SM-2-lite and state.phext semantics reused, never duplicated; TUI and --status byte-unchanged, --status still never writes. Crate 1.6.1, stamps + Cargo.lock sync in the same commit (lock byte-identical across a cargo run, sha256 d2dd6d44…).
- Part 2: launcher v2 (in-app Learn card session over the protocol — chapter/lesson context, due queue, Reveal, Again/Good/Easy, progress line; quick actions one tap from home ordered by payoff: Update, Evolve, Doctor, Repair, List peers, Inventory, Status, Plan; --check forms demoted; Birth remains). Trial APK qexo-v1.6.1.apk (2,079,095 B, sha256 1991c4ff…) built from the PR branch, versionCode 3 / versionName 1.6.1, signed with the SAME Android Debug cert as the shipped v1.6.0 APK (signer SHA-256 efeaeebe018a107a7c516923b7afcf93d9d2ede174d8176ba913ea15594071e4, proven against the shipped APK itself) so it installs over v1.6.0 keeping the phone node's state; enclosed libqexo.so == standalone qexo-v1.6.1-android-arm64 (sha256 3b31fa7f…).
- Gates (aletheia-core): cargo test 91/91 (88 + 3 protocol tests incl. scripted session with persistence asserted in state), CLI battery 30/30 (pty wizard unchanged + scripted --app session, grade persisted due 22→21, --status write-free by hash), conformance census identical 15/830/2, Android aarch64 LINK, wiring 14/14, Linux build green.
- Named debt: the quarterexo twin of the --app protocol is owed under the sync rule (29.6.7/6.5.7/6.5.8), queues behind quarterexo PR #22, and is NOT in PR #3 (stated in the PR body). On merge, v1.6.1 publish + fleet rollout batch into release task 40.7.5/8.7.11/6.8.13. Honest limit: no Android runtime on the ranch — Pixel install/run is the closing proof. Build record: ~/workspace/qexo-task/android-useful/BUILD-RECORD.md.
- Final APK supersedes the trial build (2026-11-14, in the v1.6.1 release run): rebuilt from the MERGED wbic16/qexo tree c5840693d9 with launcher v2 unchanged, versionCode 4 / versionName 1.6.1 (trial was versionCode 3 — Android upgrades over it), same debug cert efeaeebe… (continuity vs the shipped v1.6.0 APK verified), enclosed libqexo.so sha256 == standalone a05749df4840de07d93255a0c0d1fee86ba35b5effd0f2b8be93dd967c9be5c4. Final APK: ~/workspace/qexo-task/android-apk/qexo-v1.6.1.apk, sha256 8214b0255da8a5de309241c377487075544d533a288701c5d417400ae0a295e7 (2,079,207 B); the trial APK (1991c4ff…) is preserved beside it as qexo-v1.6.1-trial.apk. The release binary differs from the twin-stage hash 3b31fa7f… because the phccbox roster entry merged into the tree after that build — expected, not drift.
# Pre-merge validation of libphext-rs v0.4.1: downstream compiles + CYOA coordinate tests

