# Thirst for Knowledge quest — daily arXiv math scan, skim-before prediction, skim calibration on the Oracle detection list

Coordinate: 30.7.8/10.6.14/5.6.10
Issued: 2026-11-09 08:22 CST
Request (verbatim): setup a thirst for knowledge quest - every day, scour https://arxiv.org/list/math/new for a new candidate paper to absorb - find a metric to measure your predictive capability - add it to the Research Oracle detection list - Skim, Before, and After
Status: in progress — quest designed, first scan dispatched 2026-11-09; charter rule 17 to follow when the tracker is free (S006 in flight)

Notes:
- DESIGN: (1) Daily scan of arxiv.org/list/math/new (new + cross-lists, not replacements); ONE candidate chosen by stated criteria (cluster proximity for measurable deltas, occasional far/axis candidate, crisp theorem-bearing abstract; 'no candidate' is an honest outcome, never force a pick). (2) SKIM-BEFORE prediction, from title+abstract only, sealed in the quest log (~/workspace/thirst-quest/, own git repo — commit timestamp is the receipt) BEFORE any full read: predicted new concepts, predicted revisions, axis-opening yes/no, predicted NI. (3) Absorb: full ingestion as the next paper. (4) AFTER score: |predicted NI - measured NI|, concept-count error, axis hit/miss. METRIC: Skim Calibration = rolling mean |NI error| over the last 10 scored papers + axis-flag accuracy — added to the Research Oracle DETECTION LIST (with NI trend and axis events): as the Oracle matures, the model should foresee a paper's delta from its abstract alone; falling skim error is the fixed point announcing itself. Protocol is universal: Will-posted papers also get a skim prediction before the full read. Studies exempt (no NI). (5) Charter rule 17 + detection-list scroll + rd-tracker skill update land via a tracker amendment pass once S006's ingestion frees the builder; daily cron 'thirst-for-knowledge' runs the loop and reports to MOAT.
- AMENDMENT (Will, 2026-11-09 08:29): for each sourced paper, estimate IMPACT before (new links internal/cross-cluster, questions opened, predicted Oracle after + range + direction, one-line expected-impact statement) and record the ACTUAL DELTA after in the same terms. Applied: daily cron body updated; prediction #1 gained a blind impact supplement (quest log commit 59f58d9 — pred 4 new links, 2 questions opened, Oracle ~38% (30-48) up modestly; expected impact: Cluster E's first refutation, possibly the tracker's first False). Will then delivered the candidate's full text himself (arxiv.org/html/2611.09694v1, 08:30) — absorption as Paper 008 queued behind S006; blind state intact (prediction + supplement committed before the link arrived; text unopened by Emise until absorption).
- LOOP RULES (Will, 2026-11-09 08:31): the quest loop is immediate and unbroken — choose, download the paper in HTML form, read it, integrate it, then journal about the PROCESS in mastery.phext. mastery.phext CREATED 2026-11-09 (canonical: ~/workspace/phext/mastery.phext; source mastery-source.json + build_mastery_phext.py; Home scroll states purpose + entry scheme — entry k at 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.(k+1)) and PUBLISHED to wbic16/agi@exo at repo root alongside research.phext et al. (commit fd84a264, parent 77629f3b, remote bytes sha256-verified f407813e...); SOURCES.md row added so the agi collection refresh covers it. Daily cron body updated with the download-HTML/integrate-immediately/journal+publish steps. First journal entry lands with Paper 008's integration.

