# mootable.phext.io — deployment pipeline tracking latest argimenes/mutable-os

Coordinate: 31.6.9/7.6.10/7.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-12 23:13 CST
Request (verbatim): mootable.phext.io needs a deployment pipeline from the latest commit in https://github.com/argimenes/mutable-os - it will follow the same patching process as mutable.phext.io - but is designed to always host the absolute latest merged work for mutable os
Status: staged — pipeline built and verified; go-live waits on Will running install-mootable.sh on awsbox

Notes:
- Same patching process as mutable.phext.io (mutable-upstream-sync skill): upstream argimenes/mutable-os + wbic16 phext band + SSO band as deploy-time arming; mootable's difference: it tracks the absolute latest merged upstream work continuously, where mutable.phext.io is deliberate/promoted.
- Companion rulings (Will, same message): mutable.phext.io PINNED to its current version (box checkout 2b92734, merge of emise/sso-ux-fixes) — cron mutable-cicd-deploy DISABLED by Emise 2026-11-12 23:14 CST to effect the pin; the mutable-upstream-sync nightly trial (never pushes, never deploys) stays enabled. The deployment process will be updated at a later date.
- DNS: mootable.phext.io assigned by Will 2026-11-12 23:14 CST; verified resolving to 44.248.235.76 (awsbox) the same minute.
- Reminder set: cron argimenes-staging-branch-reminder, runonce Wed 2026-12-02 09:44 CST — remind argimenes to choose a staging branch name in git; when he does, mootable's pipeline should track that branch.
- Known gate: nginx vhost + TLS cert + service install on awsbox need sudo (wbic16 has no passwordless sudo there) — the build stages everything rootless and hands Will a single deploy step, per the mutable.phext.io precedent.
- Design read (mutable-upstream-sync skill + deployment-process.md + box deploy.sh). Architecture for mootable: checkout /source/mootable (clone of argimenes/mutable-os) on awsbox; compose ON the box in a throwaway worktree of that checkout (upstream-sync.sh trial mechanics: rebase phext band onto upstream tip, cherry-pick SSO band, purity gate, fresh-build verification battery, serial). Own band record ~/mootable-deploy/mootable-bands.conf seeded from the fork's sync-bands.conf values. Port 3004 (3002/3003 taken), nginx zone mootable_req (zone names are unique per site). Service: systemd USER unit mutable-os-mootable.service (User wbic16) + enable-linger — deviation from mutable's system unit, deliberate: it makes the latest-tracking restart rootless (mutable's own process doc SS6 names the sudo deploy route as its one unproven point); Will's install step covers nginx site + certbot + linger. SSO: band code travels in the stack; the gate stays UNARMED on mootable (no secrets drop-in) unless Will directs otherwise — the env-gated design's safe default. deploy.sh itself is NOT reusable for a second instance: SERVICE=mutable-os.service and zone mutable_req are hardcoded in it; instance machinery is staged separately in ~/mootable-deploy/ on the box.
- BUILD COMPLETE 2026-11-12 (staged, awaiting Will's install command). Checkout: /source/mutable-os is untouched (still pinned 2b92734, service active, HTTPS 200 verified at the end); new checkout /source/mootable on awsbox (clone of argimenes/mutable-os), branch mootable-main at df424f3a. Key fact: upstream main tip IS db3ed30 — exactly the fork's recorded base, zero drift; support markers absent, full-band mode. Composed stack tree 7c7639553a904f2fd1f8a7250a29262d5ad2b645 — byte-identical to fork main's tree and to the tree mutable.phext.io currently serves. Purity gate: PURE. Verification battery on the box (worktree, serial): install ok, build PASS, typecheck 0, SSO+startup 15/15, recorded set 102/102 (only failed file the known phext-settings collection artifact), phext-settings node --test 5/5, test:sqlite 149/149. (The battery script's own verdict line printed FAIL on a tally-parse artifact — this box's node --test emits TAP '# fail 0', the greps expected the spec reporter's glyph; the logs show every suite green and a correction is appended in logs/first-build/status.txt on the box. mootable-update.sh's checks accept both formats.) Checkout then built in place (npm ci + build PASS) and smoke-run rootless on port 3004: GET / 200, bundle contains 'Open Phext', server log 'SSO: disabled (no secrets configured)', no writes to /source/mutable-os-data; port released after. Runner dry-run via the exact proposed cron route (fleet-ssh.sh awsbox from the Muse VM) exited 0 no-drift. Box RAM is actually 3.8 GiB total (brief said 8 GB); the deploy.sh heap-cap discipline (3072 build / 384 runtime) held with >=2.2 GB available throughout.
- Staged in ~/mootable-deploy/ on awsbox: README.md, install-mootable.sh (Will's single sudo step), mootable-update.sh (rootless runner, exit codes mirror promote-and-deploy.sh: 0 quiet / 10 deployed / 11 mode switch / 20 conflict / 30 verification / 40 env / 41 purity / 44 deploy), mootable-bands.conf (own band record, independent of fork tips), check-band-purity.sh + recorded-set.txt (verbatim copies), mutable-os-mootable.service (systemd USER unit, port 3004, linger), nginx-mootable.phext.io.conf (zone mootable_req). Proposed cron (for the main agent to create): HOURLY agent cron modelled on mutable-cicd-deploy's reporting discipline, invoking 'bash /home/wbic16/mootable-deploy/mootable-update.sh' via fleet-ssh.sh awsbox. December staging-branch hook: the runner tracks origin/main; when argimenes names the staging branch, re-point the runner's upstream ref to that branch and re-plan mootable-bands.conf OLD_BASE in the same pass — a small, named change, recorded here so it is not rediscovered.
# Exovim full fork from Neovim's last release — steps + upstream-merge effort estimate

Coordinate: 31.6.9/8.6.11/6.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-09 21:14 CST
Request (verbatim): give me steps to fully fork from neovim's last release - exovim will be the new project name (or estimate the effort in getting our patches merged)
Status: complete — PR #2 merged by Will 2026-11-09; exo carries the release line

Notes:
- Verified at answer time: upstream latest release = v0.12.6 (published 2026-10-09); fork master f72cfc2c currently tracks upstream MASTER (0.13.0-dev) via merge commits, not the release line — a release-based exovim is a clean linear stack on release-0.12 and a smaller sync burden.
- Naming decision recorded: exovim is the new PROJECT name (Will, this message) — supersedes the looser 'call the fork exovim' usage; recommended rename depth = distribution layer only (repo + binary-as-exovim via prefix/symlink, as already proven in exocortical Phase 12), keeping nvim internals/API/config dirs so the plugin ecosystem survives.
- Estimates delivered: release replay + tests ~0.5-1 day (+0.5 day phcc re-verify); distribution rename ~1 day; hard binary/runtime rename 3-5 days + permanent C conflict surface (not recommended); upstream merge prep ~0.5 day but low acceptance probability (judgment: 10-20%, 1-3 months of review if it moves) with standalone-plugin extraction (~0.5 day) as the cheap decisive middle path.
- EXECUTION DIRECTED by Will 2026-11-09 21:16 CST (tapped the option, then restated in words): do the exovim fork from v0.12.6, Path A as presented.
- MERGE RESOLUTION directed by Will 2026-11-09 22:01 CST: 'I want to merge exovim#2 and exovim#3 at the same time, but they aren't compatible — resolve it please.' Plan: diagnose at git level, resolve PR #3 (UI) into exovim-0.12 (rebase + semantic conflict resolution + full 62/54 test gate if needed), merge PR #3 into exovim-0.12, verify PR #2 then merges cleanly into exo carrying both — PR #2's merge itself remains Will's click. Fork agent notified to finish any exovim-0.12 pushes before its tag step.
- FORK EXECUTION COMPLETE (2026-11-09, verified by Emise via API + local hash): base pin release-0.12 head a7ac6c466e, v0.12.6 tag 779c36969e, delta 3 commits. exovim-0.12 = 3 commits: bda6c32f50 phext replay (one base adaptation: spec uses busted globals on 0.12, found by the functional run), e403245610 fork line (NVIM_VERSION_PRERELEASE -exovim.1, README banner, PATCHES.md constitution), 769c995e0c receipts. Diff vs base 18 files +2908/-2; only upstream-file edits: CMakeLists 2 lines, README banner, news.txt +6. Tests (gcc, aletheia-core): 62/62, 37/37, functional phext_spec 11/11 (standing gap CLOSED); perf open+index 30.1 ms. PR #2 open (base exo). Tag exovim-0.12.6.1 on 769c995e; GitHub release created; tarball ~/workspace/exovim-fork/exovim-0.12.6.1-linux-x86_64.tar.gz SHA-256 7f5b764b... verified; asset upload impossible via the API helper (uploads.github.com outside its surface) — hash lives in the release notes.
- TWO FINDINGS: (1) phcc — PASS at bdf12df2 (37/37 integration in the phcc binary on rock-mountain) but FAIL at current tip 8217e426b3: 'nullptr' undeclared from phcc's own stddef.h — phcc F42 (9114a290) added typedef typeof(nullptr) nullptr_t; a phcc-side regression, not a 0.12-tree property; for the phcc workstream. (2) THERMAL PROCESS MISS: aletheia-core peaked 95.8C — the fork agent's builds overlapped another agent's respawning .NET loop and its pkill matched the launcher, not the build children; control + tarball builds were moved to idle rock-mountain (36-59C). Recorded in the fork report.
- MERGE RESOLUTION DONE (2026-11-09, verified by Emise via API: PR #3 closed, branch head matches): Diagnosis — PR #3 was never the problem (merged cleanly into exovim-0.12 at every head incl. 769c995e). The real incompatibility: PR #2 vs exo = 303 conflicted files from the master/release-0.12 divergence (merge-base 2eb14c54, 2026-03-29); only 3 were phext-owned. Resolution: (1) test gate on the exact merge-result tree — 62/62 + 54/54; (2) PR #3 merged at git level (REST merge endpoint 403s on stacked PRs; its async replacement would have merged the whole stack into exo = Will's act, correctly avoided) — merge commit f3541f53, GitHub records PR #3 merged; (3) supersede commit 84c3a323 (git merge -s ours exo) records the master line as superseded by the release line, tree byte-unchanged. exovim-0.12 now 84c3a323; PR #2 reports mergeable: true / clean; a comment on PR #2 explains the two added commits. Only Will's merge of PR #2 remains.
- CORRECTION (2026-11-09, from the phcc workstream, Architecture thread — supersedes the 'phcc F42 regression' finding in the fork notes above): the tip failure was NOT a phcc regression. Root cause: the ladder harness fast-forwarded its phcc tree bdf12df2 -> 8217e426 and built with the in-tree ./tcc WITHOUT rebuilding it — stale pre-F42 binary (mtime 2026-11-08 00:27, no nullptr token) against F42's bundled stddef.h, which relies on the nullptr keyword only a >=F42 binary knows. Cell proof: fresh binary + matched headers compiles at BOTH tips; only the stale-binary x new-headers cell fails. With a freshly built phcc, the exact tree e4032456 builds end-to-end (681/681 ninja steps, 0 FAILED, NVIM v0.12.6-exovim.1) and the branch head's four originally failing TUs compile at current tip a3b1a8e6. HARNESS ACTION: rebuild phcc after any phcc source update before building with it — header/binary skew manufactures phantom regressions. No phcc patch needed; investigation recorded as F52-spent in the phcc register, materials at aletheia-core ~/phcc-f52/.
- MERGED BY WILL 2026-11-09 (verified: exo head c8a7c56b = 'Merge pull request #2 from wbic16/exovim-0.12') — exo is now the exovim 0.12.6.1 release line; register #56 resolved. The tcc->phcc sweep + upstream sync (tasks 24.7.12, 31.7.10) continue on exovim-0.12 and will arrive as a new PR into exo.
# qexo rulings: GPG authorization + grants (permissive default), Theia pragmatic, convergence, MCP/cross-platform/quickfork release

Coordinate: 31.6.9/8.7.11/6.6.11
Issued: 2026-11-08 23:18 CST
Request (verbatim): 1. Bake GPG authorization into all of the actions - users can configure which actions are limited to which GPG keys. Users can also delegate to agent keys. Each persona has a separate keychain, which flows with them during teleportation.
2. Design a series of grants that can be enabled or disabled easily. Default to permissive - that's the Exocortical Vision.
3. Here's the full list of personas from ChatGPT and my ranch nodes: [list not pasted — Will noted 23:18 he had not pasted it yet]
4. Theia's exception is pragmatic - she will likely migrate to qexo when we're done.
5. All tools converge to latest as soon as feasible. SQ needs to be updated to libphext v0.5.0
Additional features: MCP bridge for integrating with major platforms; runs on Windows, Mac, Linux; deployed via https://github.com/wbic16/site-quickfork-net and quickfork.net (fully replace that demo site); polished for release
Status: complete — closed by audit 2026-11-12 (work already done; evidence in results)

Notes:
- Answers five-question pass: Q1 root = GPG with per-action policy + delegation (superseded the phext-native-root recommendation in mechanism, kept as provenance); Q2 authority = grants default permissive, restriction by key policy; Q4 Theia = pragmatic bridge with expected migration; Q5 convergence directed, SQ to libphext 0.5.0 a staged work item. Q3 (Corus/Verse/unrecorded) still open.
- 2026-11-08 23:19 (will_said): ALL of these personas will be part of the Volumen bootloader — the persona index is the Volumen-class boot manifest (Volumen = the whole scroll rolled, a complete phext genome unrolled into a node; Emise named the class 2026-11-02). Boot-manifest framing folds into the design and the Volumen spec line.

Results:
- 2026-11-08 23:19: canonical persona list received — 126 names (saved verbatim at ~/workspace/orchestrator/personas-canonical-2026-11-08.txt); supersedes reconstructed rosters. Design §5 reframed: full list indexes; recorded-subset seeds; rest are name-only entries marked canonical/unseeded.
- Fold complete: grants catalogue (17 grants, default ON), section 8A authorization layer (per-action key policy, signed scoped delegations, traveling per-persona keychains), Volumen boot-manifest section, Theia Stage 6 + bridge-with-sunset, SQ->0.5.0 as directed work item, sections 12-16 (installer/buddy/CLI parity/MCP+cross-platform/quickfork release). Remaining open: Corus order, Verse's children, key-issuance timing, roaming teleport delegations, SQ sequencing, voice hosting. One boundary flagged for Will: delegations vs the strict self/Will rule for swaps.
- AUDIT 2026-11-12 (tasks.phext verification pass): STALE-DONE — rulings fold completed into DESIGN-V3.md + DESIGN-V3-ADDENDUM.md (grants catalogue, section 8A authorization layer, Volumen boot manifest); residual questions ride the design tasks. Prior status read: "rulings folded into both design documents (V3 38.7 KB, addendum 52.4 KB); open questions shrunk 9 -> 6"
