# Fix edit.phext.io footer overflow on live v1.1.0

Coordinate: 31.7.7/7.6.11/6.5.10
Issued: 2026-11-09
Request (from session record): footer issues - it runs off the page - testing mcp now
Status: DONE — PR #49 merged by Will 2026-11-09 23:55:22 CST (merge 327fa929), in exo head c5da01ee, ships in v1.1.1. Root cause (measured): signed-in status-bar row ~2,201px min-content inside overflow-clip ancestors + dead height:auto in the 701-1100px band. Fix: 3 CSS lines (flex-wrap + min-height on base #status-bar rule, dead band height removed, MCP code overflow-wrap:anywhere) + regression test status_bar_wraps_instead_of_running_off_the_page. Counts lib 183/0, bin 81/0. Architecture chat's separate footer/wiki task (31.5.8/6.5.10/4.4.10) had NOT landed by 00:01 CST — no wiki-access change in v1.1.1; their worker warned it must rebase onto c5da01ee (status bar already fixed) to avoid a duplicate #status-bar edit.
# Independently verify 358 vs 370 (helios_stalled_parse)

Coordinate: 31.7.8/10.7.12/6.6.10
Issued: 2026-11-07 00:10 CST
Request (verbatim): see if you can independently verify which value is correct, and why the test is wrong
Status: complete — Will confirmed the Linux/Windows reading and directed handling both values; fix committed on provable-0.4.1, suite fully green (58/58)

Notes:
- Ground truth from raw bytes (Python scan, not the Rust parser): fixture blob (git object, 14,035 B, sha256 3a7c29bf…) has first 0x17 at offset 358; segment pure ASCII, 358 B = 358 chars. Fixture byte-identical at b5a8c5d and 84a8ae9. At b5a8c5d (2025-01-10) the test expected 358 and 15150; commit 84a8ae9 (2025-01-25, explode/implode) edited ONLY the expectations to 370 / 15317. Deltas: 370-358=12 = LF count in first scroll; 15317-15150=167 = 159 LF (helios) + 8 LF (msg). Mechanism: test reads working-tree files; on a CRLF (Windows autocrlf) checkout every LF gains a byte, and the constants were re-typed from that run's own println output. No .gitattributes pins fixture eol. Proof by restoration: scratch copy with 358/15150 passes the full test (Helios: 358). This settles the factual half of the long-open helios adjudication (goal_c99cb0d5342d); fix ready to ride the provable-0.4.1 PR as its own commit.
- FIX (Will, 2026-11-07 00:19: 'the tests pass on windows - we should probably just handle both values'): helios_stalled_parse now asserts 358||370 and 15150||15317 with the CRLF explanation inline; commit on branch provable-0.4.1 in ~/workspace/libphext-provable/libphext-rs; cargo test = 58 passed, 0 failed — first fully green run on Linux.
