Status: COMPLETE: wbic16/phcc main+exo @ 395f5d63; backup branch emise/pre-slice0-2026-11-07 @ 1b102067 preserved; fresh-clone ranch build ALL TESTS PASSED.

Results:
- wbic16/phcc main+exo @ 395f5d631ab8ee5659d7815adcb1f96237c40658; backup branch preserves old main 1b102067.
passed# qexo v1.0.3 forecast gate fix: forecast the node's configured lenses, not the legacy VM ceilings

Coordinate: 31.7.10/8.6.11/6.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-12 23:31 CST
Request (from session record): PR #10 (v1.0.2) replaced the disk gate with a volume lens + optional quota lens but left the forecast projecting the legacy absolute levels (byte AMBER 95 GB / RED 102 GB). Fleet evidence from the 2026-11-12 rollout: the second plan read on any ranch node flipped to FORECAST AMBER (95 GB projected in 0.0 days) over a GREEN gate. Fix: forecast crossings computed against the same configured lenses (volume free-fraction levels of the node's own volume; quota only when on, named as quota; file thresholds from config); legacy levels deleted from the forecast path; already-reached crossings belong to the gate, not projected at 0.0 d; projections bounded to a one-year horizon.
Status: MERGED 2026-11-12 (PR #12, merged_at 2026-11-13T05:39:19Z; exo head 1b819c2e). v1.0.3 forecast fix is on exo. Fleet nodes still run the v1.0.2 binary (gate-correct; forecast fix not yet rolled out — Will's call).

Results:
- Branch emise/forecast-gate-v1.0.3 @ 889da9b698a770440f5ece852a06c8a709dc29ad, parent 7bfc03cb (fresh at push), force disabled, remote tree verified 37/37 blobs+modes; diff vs v1.0.2 = 8 files.
- Gates (aletheia-core): cargo test 36/36 (33 + 3 new: ranch regression, filling-volume volume-RED, quota-named-quota); release build OK; wiring-check OK.
- Two-run CLI repro on the incident volume: run 2 stays GREEN, forecast reports no crossing — no FORECAST AMBER flip.
# Merge upstream into the exovim fork (release-0.12 line)

