Notes:
- Will, MOAT, 2026-11-11 00:44 CST. Sub-task of the phextura line (27.6.7/7.6.10/7.5.10). Coordinator dispatched: choose one of the 12 tracker-ingested arXiv papers, encode it as a phextura corpus per DESIGN.md, render an HTML reading view by coordinate traversal (demo harness, not the product), one-pass reference validation (zero dangling = publishable to wbic16/phextura examples/), and a friction log - math entry handling is INTERIM by definition and must be flagged with costs.
- COMPLETED 2026-11-11 01:00 CST. Paper chosen: arXiv:2611.08794 (tracker P010, Onsager correction) - hardest fetchable exercise: 16 books, 37 theorem-class blocks, 637 display equations, 39 bib entries, 9 SVG figures (text-native, embedded literally, zero placeholders). Corpus 2611.08794.phext: 1,154 scrolls, 1,421,714 bytes. Validation: 780 coordinate references, 780 resolved, 0 dangling; coverage audit caught 235 LaTeXML duplicate equations and a float dual-identity bug before final. Rendered HTML (demo harness, not the product): all 3,710 fragment links resolve, display numbers render-time only. Published to wbic16/phextura@exo examples/2611.08794/, commit 2b3909a67b658562cbf3b42ff6f33d2e3a388593, blob hashes verified. Friction log F1-F11 at ~/workspace/phextura-design/demo/friction.md; F1 (math interim inherits LaTeX, preamble macros homeless) feeds the notation session; F2-F5 fed into the design loop's Pass 3 the same night.
