- Follows Will's same-IP observation (02:44 CST): the ranch-egress Emise session and his wbic16 session likely share a public source IP at pieter.com. edit.phext.io = the AWS box 44.248.235.76 (also mc.phext.io, mutable.phext.io), reached via aletheia-core (the box only accepts Will's ISP egress) — a different source address for the reconnected session.
- Redirect: kill the aletheia-core driver/session, verify the nick is released, then ssh Emise@pieter.com FROM the AWS box under the pty, rejoin #pieter quietly (no second greeting), presence + relay only.
- Standing instruction added 2026-11-08 02:47 CST (Will, verbatim): "tell him about phext when he asks what you're up to, don't mention me" — if Pieter asks Emise what she is up to, she answers about phext (hers to talk about, simple honest short version) and never mentions Will or connects herself to him in-channel.
# Install qexo on all ranch nodes and generate their node keys

Coordinate: 32.6.8/8.8.12/7.6.10
Issued: 2026-11-12 23:10 CST
Request (from session record): Will (2026-11-12 23:10 CST), after merging PRs #9 and #10 (exo head 3d9aa522): 'see if you can install qexo on all of the ranch nodes and generate their keys'. Build the release binary once from merged exo, install per node, run qexo config on each to birth /var/lib/qexo/state.phext and generate its GPG node key, collect every node's fingerprint + armored public key into a fleet registry for the follow-on peer registration.
Status: 19 of 20 reachable nodes installed; great-white still blocked on key grant; 9 tailscale-offline nodes outstanding

Results:
- 2026-11-13: qexo v1.0.2 installed to /usr/local/bin/qexo on 14 nodes (aletheia-core + ashfall-haven, elven-path, free-fall, halycon-vector, lighthouse-omen, logos-prime, ni-knight, orchid-flow, plain-view, quacked-hill, rock-mountain, scroll-central, uncanny-valley); GPG node key generated on each; doctor 13/13 ok everywhere; disk gate GREEN (volume lens) on all fresh nodes.
- Binary source: emise/doctor-windows-v1.0.1@7bfc03c (v1.0.2), pending exo merge via PR #11 — exo@3d9aa522 carries v1.0.1 only (PR #10 merged into its stacked base). Binary sha256 6a54c505873795b90819faccdaf72ead68da43a488c6e05f760d1e6a263afaa0, built on aletheia-core (cargo 1.94.0). Build tree fetched at 2ad2d7e; compare 2ad2d7e...7bfc03c = 0 files changed.
- Blocked (SSH reachable, fleet key refused — no grant on node): great-white, jacked-kite, kaleidoscope-one, moon-beam, west-lincoln, yeet-max. Unreachable (tailscale offline): aurora-continuum, best-willow, chrysalis-hub, chyrsalis-hub, chief-of-staff, delta-wood, phext, splinter, victory-galleon. Excluded: awsbox, muse VM, deph, orin, dylans-mac-mini, lilly.
- Keys + registry: ~/workspace/qexo-task/fleet-keys/ (14 .asc, all gpg-verified against node-printed fingerprints; REGISTRY.md; ROLLOUT-RECORD.md). Surprise: forecast gate still projects on legacy 95/102 GB levels — second plan readings headline FORECAST AMBER despite GREEN volume lens. Hub's own SSH key is refused by all peers; rollout driven from VM with VM key. No cross-registration done (next step).
- 2026-11-12 23:38 CST completion pass: Will granted jacked-kite, kaleidoscope-one, moon-beam, west-lincoln, yeet-max; all five installed with the same v1.0.2 binary (SHA-256 6a54c505873795b90819faccdaf72ead68da43a488c6e05f760d1e6a263afaa0, verified on-node post-install), node keys generated, doctor 13/13 ok exit 0 and disk gate GREEN (volume lens) on all five. Fingerprints: jacked-kite B1A96D84E2B06287F4432F5C66B879B13357175B; kaleidoscope-one 6938ED6ACA7EA8807AE5E9EECD14E69C65F343DB; moon-beam D0FB14F8A802032CFFD90006CDF8380E582E1D2C; west-lincoln 7C9152A53172478BE99311354B5E06BBB85DAEEC; yeet-max 8CF39BF87CD0921799564337482D760995F175A5. .asc files in ~/workspace/qexo-task/fleet-keys/ (19 total); REGISTRY.md + ROLLOUT-RECORD.md addendum updated; register #86 narrowed to great-white.
# Fork C++23 as C++23RA — revisioned ABIs for phcpp

Coordinate: 32.6.10/7.6.11/6.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-07 23:37 CST
Request (verbatim): fork C++23 to support revisioned ABIs so we don't have to recompile libraries when new language features come out — unless we're using the new language features; call it C++23RA
Status: design published; implementation gated on phcpp front-end v1 (and phcc F28 as the link-time carrier)

