# Platform-stamped signed manifests + APK bundle support on full nodes — phones upgrade through the phextnet

Coordinate: 34.8.11/8.7.11/7.7.9
Issued: 2026-11-13 01:12 CST
Request (from session record): Surfaced by the Android port (wbic16/qexo PR #1): the v1.1.0 release manifest carries version/sha256/size but no platform, and the fleet signer (aletheia-core) announces x86_64 builds. Android nodes are protected tonight only by the version rule (phone at 1.3.0 > offered 1.2.0) plus swap post-check + rollback. Proper fix in quarterexo: add a platform field to the signed manifest (e.g. linux-x86_64 / android-arm64 / windows-x86_64), have release stamp the build's platform, and assess_offer refuse cross-platform offers BEFORE download. Signer may announce multiple platform manifests in the releases family.
Status: spec drafted 2026-11-14 (~/workspace/qexo-task/apk-updates/SPEC.md) — awaiting build dispatch behind quarterexo PR #22 merge

Notes:
- EXPANDED SCOPE (Will, 2026-11-14 03:07 CST): beyond the platform field — full nodes (quarterexo builds) BUNDLE APK support: a release announcement can carry the Android APK as the android-arm64 artifact alongside linux-x86_64 / windows-x86_64 binaries; serve delivers the APK over the phextnet; an Android node's update flow fetches the APK offer, verifies signature + sha256 under the same assess_offer trust rules (cross-platform offers refused BEFORE download), and hands the verified APK to the Android install path. Phones then upgrade to latest through the same signed channel as every other node — no manual APK ferrying. Version slice: v1.7.0, quarterexo first, synced to wbic16/qexo per the two-repo rule (29.6.7/6.5.7/6.5.8). Spec first (spec-only pass dispatched 2026-11-14); build dispatch waits for PR #22 (internal OpenPGP — the phone-side verifier) to land in quarterexo.
- SPEC (2026-11-14): ~/workspace/qexo-task/apk-updates/SPEC.md — build-ready v1.7.0 design grounded in the v1.6.0 tree. Key decisions: ONE signed manifest scroll per announcement (primary artifact in the top-level fields exactly as today + `platform:` line + `artifact:` stanzas for the rest; one signature covers all, old binaries read the primary and behave as today, legacy platform-less manifests match linux-x86_64 only with a printed note); platform tokens linux-x86_64 / windows-x86_64 / android-arm64 (raw Termux binary) / android-arm64-apk; signer bundles via `qexo release [--apk <path>] [--artifact <platform>:<path>]` with canonical names in releases/ (serve byte route needs NO change — qexo-<version>.apk already passes its predicate); selection inserted in update_inner AFTER signature verification and BEFORE version judgment, so cross-platform offers are refused pre-download (NoArtifactForPlatform, no receipt); APK form applies by verify→stage→pending-install marker→launcher Install button→system installer, with a settle step writing the closing `applied` receipt (binary swap is structurally impossible inside the APK — nativeLibraryDir is not writable). Two open questions for Will ride in the spec: APK signing-key adoption (debug key vs a real keystore now) and whether the first 1.7.0 announcement carries the windows .exe.
