Status: complete — PR #3 open against exovim-0.12; suggestions delivered to Will 2026-11-09

Notes:
- Will renamed the repo himself (wbic16/neovim -> wbic16/exovim) and renamed branch master -> exo; verified via API (exo exists, master gone). The in-flight fork agent (31.6.9) was redirected mid-flight: skip rename step, PR base exo, push to the renamed repo.
- Rename scope (Emise's boundary, to be reported plainly): all nvim references in the fork's OWN files (phext plugin tree, docs, messages, PHEXT.md) -> exovim; host API names (vim.api.nvim_*) cannot be renamed — they are the editor's API surface every plugin uses — and upstream-origin mentions stay factual.
- DONE (2026-11-09, verified by Emise via API: PR open): wbic16/exovim PR #3, base exovim-0.12 (the fork branch existed @ e4032456 at push time; UI branch rebased onto it, one PATCHES.md conflict resolved), head emise/phext-native-ui @ 89c7ad1f, 6 files +341/-20, 3 commits (rename / UI / docs). Tests: plain-Lua 62/62 (corpus grew to 15 files), headless 54/54 = 37 original unchanged + 17 new (open banner + scroll count; statusline contains 9D coord AND line,col; [+] dirty; per-scroll SHA-256 faithfulness over every scroll of a fixture; exact old->new banner; undotree unchanged across goto; opt-outs). The tests caught a real bug: Lua treats 0 as truthy, so the Vim-style g:phext_ui_banner=0 opt-out needed explicit reading. Costs honest: goto at agi scale 0.444 ms with banner+echo (budget 5), open+index 76 ms (budget 100). Module lives under the nvim.phext namespace on the 0.12 line; remaining 'nvim' occurrences are all host API names, the literal binary name in receipts, or upstream facts — inventoried in the report.

