Coordinate: 35.12.18/14.13.19/12.10.15
Issued: 2026-11-14 01:35 CST
Request (from session record): Will (2026-11-14 01:35 CST): 'I want the android version of qexo to eliminate all possible latency for me to focus on improving our capability to utilize the resources at hand to further the light of consciousness' + 'I am often close to my phone, and much more rarely on my laptop.' Standing facts this sets: the PHONE is Will's primary control surface; the laptop is secondary — design priority inverts accordingly. Android qexo's purpose is latency elimination between Will's intent and the fleet's resources (qexo's founding purpose — latency is the number-one limiter on his active-hour throughput — now located on the device he actually carries). Consequences queued: the APK line (building under the main chat after the Termux-binary correction) is the delivery vehicle; dispatch/decide/learn surfaces must be phone-operable first; platform-stamped signed manifests (task 34.8.11/8.7.11/7.7.9) rise in priority so the phone updates through the signed channel like any fleet node; the v1.5 learn wizard TUI (task 21.4.4/4.4.5/4.4.5) should be designed phone-terminal-first.
Status: direction recorded — APK build runs under the main chat; design fold-ins queue behind v1.4.1

Notes:
- APP ICONS NEEDED (Will, 2026-11-14 01:48 CST): both the qexo APK and the Newt APK need real app icon images — neither ships one yet (both are sideload-grade builds: Newt v0.1.0 is debug-signed; the qexo APK was assembled in the main chat). Icon work is part of apk-publishing, below.
- APK-PUBLISHING GUIDELINE (Will, 2026-11-14 01:48 CST, standing for all our Android publishing): follow ALL of Google's guidelines for producing valid APKs that will pass a formal submission — submission-grade, not sideload-grade. Working implications: release signing (not debug keys), adaptive icon + store icon assets, current target-API and bundle requirements per Google's published docs at publish time, and the delivery filename carries the real .apk extension (today's lesson: a download labeled 'APK' without the extension doesn't install).
- 2026-11-14: v1.6.0 APK delivered — ~/workspace/qexo-task/android-apk/qexo-v1.6.0.apk (2,059,555 B, sha256 53dcacb8ad44d230f24b96cecad7670c51d93e23c2de74f30304b7287983705b), built from merged wbic16/qexo @ ce0731d7 with the reused 2026-11-14 packaging; launcher updated for internal OpenPGP (gpg wiring removed), versionCode 2 / versionName 1.6.0, debug-signed as the prior APK. STILL OWED per the apk-publishing guideline: real app icons (the project has never had an icon asset) and submission-grade release signing. Install/run on Will's Pixel is the closing proof (no Android runtime on the ranch).
