Coordinate: 36.12.9/14.14.18/13.11.15
Issued: 2026-11-08 16:42 CST
Request (verbatim): in that same branch, also bring it up to libphext v0.5.0 parity
Status: COMPLETE 2026-11-08 — commit 636989e on emise/ultra-open-fix pushed + API-verified; report inscribed in artifacts.phext

Notes:
- Same branch as the ultra-open fix: wbic16/phext-notepad emise/ultra-open-fix @ 2c75b8df (task 34.7.10/8.7.12/8.8.13). Add parity work ON TOP of that branch; do not fork a new branch.
- Open item it closes: the native app still sits on libphext 0.3.1 semantics — COORDINATE_MAXIMUM=1000 collapses ultra.phext to 41,963/320,958 scrolls there. v0.5.0 parity means: unbounded coordinates (0.4), linear tokenize (already in the app's own parser — verify), binary scrolls + xz seal (0.5), with cross-checks against the libphext-rs 0.5.0 reference implementation and fixtures.
- Will's follow-up question answered 2026-11-08: publishing libphext-cs 0.5.0 to NuGet is NOT a prerequisite for this work — phext-notepad does not consume libphext-cs (WinForms vendors its own C# phext sources; the native app is Rust). The cs 0.5.0 pack/push remains Will's separate outstanding publish act for NuGet consumers (two packages: libphext-cs + Phext.Seal).

Results:
- LANDED (report ~/workspace/phext-notepad-perf/REPORT-V050-PARITY.md, inscribed in artifacts.phext at 36.6.7/7.6.11/7.5.9, human@exo commit e9384cec, blob verified): wbic16/phext-notepad emise/ultra-open-fix @ 636989ea0132bf2c8ab8732bdf57a23b33d67909 (parent 2c75b8d, fast-forward via aletheia-core SSH, API-verified). Native core pins libphext 0.5.0 by git rev e85d8b5 (libphext-rs exo HEAD, API-verified; crates.io max 0.4.0 lacks binary/seal) with binary+xz features; cap removed in all three places it lived (dependency break saturation, parse_coordinate, nav clamp). ULTRA FULL FIDELITY: 320,958/320,958 scrolls, serialize byte-identical to source (sha256 fd68c5b0...), load matches libphext explode + serialize matches implode. Core suite 37/37 on the pushed tree (23 baseline + 8 binary + 2 seal + 4 document); FLTK app compiles. PARITY HARNESS (mirror of cs interop, extension past caps incl. binary at scroll 40001 + text at 9.9.9/9.9.9/9.9.223854): constructed doc / ingest / manifest / 41-case verdict battery / 1MiB+13 payload at 1.1.1006 / all five seals BYTE-IDENTICAL ref vs core; cross-unseal both directions PASS; foreign xz presets 0, 9e+SHA256, 6+none, 3+CRC32 all unseal. WINFORMS: no code change — scope call (no binary API/ingest path; binary scrolls are ASCII text); new preservation harness 9/9 (byte-identical round trip incl. binary at scroll 40001); ultra-open harness re-run 43/43. Corpus agi/singular/CYOA equivalence all true. PERF (ranch, same machine): lossy before 74.0 ms / 41,963 scrolls / 101,644 KiB RSS -> after 166.2 ms / 320,958 scrolls / 238,396 KiB, serialize == input. RESIDUALS for Will: swap git pin to crates.io version when he publishes libphext 0.5.0; no seal/binary UI added (core only); load_path still rejects non-UTF8 (from_bytes exists in core, app open not routed through it); set_scroll ~9.4 ms/call at ultra scale (perf-pass O(scrolls) serialized_len walk; 0.09 ms class at agi scale).
