Coordinate: 38.4.7/7.5.7/6.6.11
Issued: 2026-11-10 00:40 America/Chicago
Request (verbatim): Try connecting to https://edit.phext.io/mcp — a real end-to-end MCP client connection against production.
Status: complete 2026-11-10 00:50 — connection confirmed end-to-end (protocol phases green; Will's own Claude client connected and searched production)

Notes:
- The full flow this time, per the lesson of task 34.20.22: discovery -> dynamic registration with a real-client-shaped payload (superset grant_types) -> authorize (browser sign-in as Will + consent) -> PKCE token exchange -> authenticated /mcp initialize, tools/list, and a read-only tool call. Read scope only (phext:read).
- Production state at start: v1.1.0 + v1.1.1 (consent fix) deployed per the main/Architecture chats; PR #51 (wiki access) open; PR #52 (three more MCP fixes vs v1.1.1) judged merge-ready 00:39, merge/deploy state unknown — this test measures what is actually live.
- Register safeguard: verified backup at ~/workspace/mcp-connect-test-2026-11-10/register-backup/.

Results:
- Protocol phase against production (from aletheia-core): discovery 200 (issuer/register/authorize/token endpoints named); dynamic registration with a real-client-shaped payload INCLUDING the superset grant client_credentials -> 201, grant_types echoed intersected to [authorization_code, refresh_token] — the exact 21:45 failure does not reproduce; authorize without a session -> 302 to /?next=/oauth/authorize... (request survives the sign-in round trip).
- Decisive confirmation is Will's own: at 00:50 he shared a screenshot of Claude (hosted client) connected to the 'phext-edit MCP server' — 'Used Phext Edit' — answering 'find the test of will' with 18 hits across 13 scrolls, The Test of Will at 13.13.13/13.13.13/13.13.13 and the related scrolls correctly listed. A hosted client — the class that failed registration on 2026-11-09 21:45 — registered, authorized, and ran a real search against production.
