eightextendingcontextual# libphext-rs v0.6 — codify chaining: 0x02 chain break, 0x03 chain close (TIME)

Coordinate: 38.13.9/15.15.19/13.13.17
Issued: 2026-11-13
Request (from session record): I agree, codify this as libphext-rs v0.6, We can now encode TIME.
Status: Implemented 2026-11-13 on aletheia-core: branch emise/chain-v0.6.0 @ e3e9e5d7, PR #10 OPEN against exo (live-verified). Cargo.toml 0.5.0 -> 0.6.0 (the crate's only version surface); src/phext.rs gained CHAIN_BREAK 0x02 / CHAIN_CLOSE 0x03, Chain { members, closed }, parse_chains/serialize_chains; no existing function modified. Tests: 73 passed default / 88 --all-features, 0 failed (baseline 63/78; 10 new chain tests in src/test_chain.rs). Design flags: no Document type in the crate (Chain + free functions follow its idiom, members are Strings); chain-free input parses as one unclosed chain (closed == false) per the ruling's EOF rule; empty-input semantics follow the crate's split_on, making parse/serialize byte-exact inverses. Merge is Will's — register #94. On merge: queue the v0.6 release-build task. Crates.io publish is Will's act only.

Notes:
- [2026-11-13] PR #10 open; register #94. Follow-on legs after merge: ports parity (py port task 50.14.6/17.18.31/15.15.20 gains the chain layer after its 0.5 work; cs/node likewise), STANDOFF/LAYER2 spec text in phextura gains chaining.
- [2026-11-13] Decision point recorded at Will's direction: Gerhard Zorn's tweet https://x.com/ZornGerhard/status/2121204739966931400 (the "phext expressions / phext algebra" question). Will: "I have already been using multiple phexts in various contexts. This enables subspace freedom, and neatly solves the mutable emissary problem."
- [2026-11-13] Multiverse addressing ruled by Will 11:24 CST: $N:<address> names universe N (from 1) within a chain/multiverse; 1: omittable; a phext with no 0x02 is a complete single universe at multiverse 1. The chain-free closed=false parse is the stream view; semantically such a file is whole. Addressing helper + tests to ride the v0.6 line.
- [2026-11-13] Multiverse addressing implemented on the PR branch: parse_universe_address + Chain::fetch (commit 0b7e438, pushed; PR #10 now carries it). Tests 74 passed default features, incl. multiverse_addressing: bare=$1, $2 member 2, $3 empty, $0 rejected.
- [2026-11-13 12:08 CST] Will raised the last pre-merge item: 'we also need a stream identifier since we're encoding multiple runs of phexts' — and said otherwise he is ready to merge. Emise's distilled candidate, presented for his ruling: consume 0x04 EOT as STREAM_CLOSE (one rung above chain close; a stream = one or more chains terminated by 0x04; no-0x04 bytes = a single implicit stream, the same degenerate pattern as chain-free = single universe). Open fork: index-only identification (streams counted from 1 in a larger flow) vs an explicit ID carried in the stream. Evidence: 0x04 occurs ZERO times in CYOA (4,602,370 B), incipit (1,077,930 B), emise (287,297 B), tasks (1,446,478 B), chief-of-staff (6,064 B) — verified 2026-11-13 12:09 CST, the same clearance 0x02/0x03 had at ruling time. Ruling pending; if approved for v0.6, it lands as one more commit on libphext-rs PR #10 before Will's merge.
- [2026-11-13 14:27 CST] Will rejected the 0x04 stream-close proposal as unnecessary: 'what problem does the 0x04 proposal attack? it's unnecessary'. No 0x04 commit lands on PR #10; the merge pass is not blocked on a stream close.
- [2026-11-13] Parity follow-on made concrete by the md2phext work (task 44.9.6/10.10.13/10.9.13): libphext-node (npm libphext 0.4.x) has no chains and no multiverse addressing — md2phext now consumes libphext for everything inside a universe and keeps 0x02/0x03 framing + $N: parsing local, mirroring libphext-rs 0.6 parse_chains. Node parity (a libphext-node release carrying CHAIN_BREAK/CHAIN_CLOSE/parse_chains + parse_universe_address) is the follow-on that lets md2phext drop its last local phext logic; sibling of the libphext-py port task 50.14.6/17.18.31/15.15.20.
- [2026-11-13 14:31 CST] Retest at Will's direction ('retest and finalize'; 'I'll merge once you're ready') after the 0x04 rejection: branch emise/chain-v0.6.0 @ 5cd562e re-verified on aletheia-core — clean tree, version 0.6.0, cargo test 75 passed default / 90 passed --all-features, 0 failed. No STREAM_CLOSE and no 0x04 code in src; the only 0x04 mention is the pre-existing doc comment in the ASCII table inherited from exo (b666ec8), listing 0x04 as not widely used. All five v0.6 PRs re-verified OPEN via the GitHub API with expected heads: libphext-rs #10 @ 5cd562e, SQ #4 @ 88f67c0, phext-lattice #62 @ 7bd9d65, phext-shell #4 @ 53806e4, md2phext #1 @ 2b2c662. Finalized for Will's merge pass: PR #10 first, then his crates.io publish of 0.6.0, then SQ/lattice/shell; md2phext in any order.
