# Image support for edit.phext.io (v1.1.0) on binary scrolls

Coordinate: 40.6.7/8.7.10/7.7.10
Issued: 2026-11-09 22:49 America/Chicago
Request (verbatim): Add image support to edit.phext.io and ship v1.1.0, using the new binary scroll capabilities.
Status: complete — closed by audit 2026-11-12 (work already done; evidence in results)

Notes:
- Binary scroll format of record (libphext-rs 0.5.0, published to crates.io 2026-11-08; Mutable embeds media this way): a binary scroll = header line 'phext-binary:1:base64' + newline + RFC 4648 base64 (padding required, no line wrapping); header alone = empty payload; header-prefixed = binary by definition; ingestion via insert_bytes/replace_bytes stores non-UTF-8 as binary scrolls of the exact bytes, never rejected. Image support must be built on THIS — no ad-hoc encoding.
- Register safeguard: verified backup at ~/workspace/image-support-v110-2026-11-09/register-backup/.

Results:
- Recon verdict: phext-lattice had NO binary-scroll support (libphext pinned 0.4.0, String-only scroll API; a canonical binary scroll would have been dumped as base64 into the editor and /api/update could mangle it). PR #45 wires in libphext 0.5.0 with the binary feature, using libphext::binary directly (no re-implementation): read_scroll_bytes/fetch_binary (well-formed decodes, else verbatim, unoccupied empty), write_binary/write_bytes (never-reject ingestion), write_scroll now refuses to replace a well-formed binary scroll with different text at the lattice layer.
- Design: per phext, image payload = binary scroll at 9.9.9/9.9.9/1.1.n, metadata JSON text scroll (name, content_type, bytes) at 9.9.9/9.9.9/1.2.n, smallest fully-free pair under the state mutex; stored filename extension forced to the sniffed type. Endpoints: POST /api/images (editor gate + CSRF, raw bytes; returns coordinate, URL, markdown reference; toolbar picker or textarea paste inserts the reference), GET|HEAD /api/media/<coord> (editor-gated) and /api/demo/media/<coord> (public) — decoded bytes, sniffed Content-Type, 404 for missing/non-binary/non-image or metadata-vs-sniff mismatch. Limits: 8 MiB/image (413 from declared length). Types: PNG/JPEG/GIF/WebP/AVIF by magic bytes only. SVG excluded entirely (415, never served) — no stored-XSS surface. Display: binary scrolls labelled in the tree, open as image+metadata (never raw base64), enterEdit and /api/update refuse them, MCP write_scroll refuses them with the reason; demo phext gained a twelfth scroll + a 1x1 GIF in demo media slot 1.
- Evidence: 266 passed / 0 failed --no-fail-fast (baseline 255; no flakes). HTTP round-trip: PNG upload -> coordinate 9.9.9/9.9.9/1.1.1 + reference; serve returns byte-identical bytes as image/png; second upload takes slot 2; a GIF named .png is stored as .gif. Refusals: anonymous 401, no-CSRF 403, non-image 415, SVG 415, oversize 413. Protection: text overwrite via /api/update and MCP both refused with bytes unmoved; no phext-binary marker or base64 appears in scroll/nav payloads for image scrolls. 8 files, +1108/-32; version bump to 1.1.0 as its own commit (3352715; crate version — the footer follows git describe, so it reads v1.1.0 once tagged).
- Honest limits (in the PR body): no MCP image tools; no image editing/resizing; no drag-and-drop (picker + paste); media scrolls join the navigation index only after the next save rebuilds it; editor/MCP search can still surface base64 fragments in result context on a matching query (search context unfiltered in this PR). Ship steps: Will merges PR #45 -> Emise tags v1.1.0 on the merged tip -> standing on-box deploy.
- AUDIT 2026-11-12 (tasks.phext verification pass): STALE-DONE — phext-lattice PR #45 MERGED (audit merge-check, 2026-11-12); v1.1.0 tagged and deployed, v1.1.1 followed (register #60 resolution). Prior status read: "PR #45 open (Emise-verified head 3352715 on exo fa8ac0d); ship = Will merges -> Emise tags v1.1.0 -> standing "
