landmarksendlessly# phcc phext capability parity with libphext-rs (C developer library)

Coordinate: 41.10.7/11.11.14/11.10.15
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (from session record): make sure phcc has every capability libphext-rs has, so developers can quickly handle phext data
Status: COMPLETE + PUBLISHED (0.5.0) — wbic16/phcc main == exo == 53a15166 (7bd02706 F45 source + 53a15166 phext refresh, on f65e68cc). Publisher verification from a fresh clone: phcc.phext sha256 9cd6bd60…, seal 59799edd…; unpack 613/613 SHA-verified; make test ALL PASSED; parity suite 163,987 checks / 0 failures under gcc with PHEXT_WITH_XZ and 163,987 / 0 under the tree's own phcc; conformance spot 332/333, diverge set exactly [a_pp_018], 0 oracle splits; static cells 3/3 (23 IRELATIVE in .rela.plt in first LOAD, static Lua byte-identical, static phccbox byte-identical, awk 42). Prior 0.4.1 state: COMPLETE + PUSHED @ 8b56ea22.

Notes:
- Phase A parity matrix: ~/workspace/phcc-libphext/PARITY.md (also committed as phext/PARITY.md). 77 capabilities audited from libphext-rs v0.4.1 source: 26 constants, 7 types, 17 Coordinate-surface items, 27 free functions - 77 with C counterparts, 0 gaps.
- Divergences of record: D-2 strict parse returns PHEXT_EFORMAT/PHEXT_ENUMBER where Rust TryFrom panics; D-3 C API byte-oriented, no UTF-8 validation; D-4 map sorted (implode identical); D-5 summary display truncation; D-6 lenient parse wraps like Rust release.
- Phase B: new top-level phext/ dir in a copy of the phcc tree on base 395f5d63 (F1) - phext.h (380 lines), phext.c (1,921 lines, incl. scalar XXH3-128 port), README, tests. Additive only; tcc.h/tccpp.c preprocessor counters untouched - wiring them to the library is the named F3-candidate follow-on, not done.
- Phase C: ported libphext-rs tests (49 test_lib + 8 test_phokenize + 1 regressions = 58 functions, same vectors): 163,831 checks, 0 failures under gcc AND under the freshly built phcc itself on aletheia-core (dogfood; phcc make test also passes). Differential fuzz vs Rust reference driver on libphext-rs 0.4.1: 40,000 cases, 2 seeds, 24 op classes, 0 divergences on defined behaviour (339 Rust panics total, all the D-2 parse class). Fuzz harness kept outside the repo at ~/workspace/phcc-libphext/fuzz/.
- Phase D: PATCHES.md gained per-file rows + entry F2. LOCAL commit 66ef47108f6580995a654a32e4ecb990b837420d on top of 395f5d63 (9 files, +4,674). NOT PUSHED - parent sequences the push (remote main has since advanced via the consolidation and pack/unpack passes, so the push will need a rebase/merge decision by the parent).
- 0.5.0 move (2026-11-08, PATCHES.md F45): re-audited against the PUBLISHED crates.io libphext 0.5.0 package (crate SHA-256 c8f8df75..., index-verified; not a git branch). Delta = 16 capabilities (binary module: 10 functions + header constant; seal module: 4 functions + SEAL_PRESET) plus one core behaviour change found by the fuzz: lenient to_coordinate now saturates at u64::MAX (0.4.1 wrapped). Totals: 93 capabilities, 93 with C counterparts, 0 gaps. New divergences D-7 (cargo feature gating mapped to build-time PHEXT_WITH_XZ for the seal; binary always compiled, base64 self-contained) and D-8 (seal io error vocabulary -> PHEXT_EINVAL/PHEXT_ENOSEAL). D-2 now only the EFORMAT/ENUMBER spelling split (0.5.0 TryFrom returns Err; fuzz op-20 panics: 0). Work on rock-mountain, base f65e68cc (cloned at D9 tip 611b763e; the h8 receipt-port commit landed during the run and was fast-forwarded to before work began). LOCAL commits 7bd02706 (F45 source) + 53a15166 (phext refresh) — coordinator publishes.

Results:
- libphext-rs 0.4.1 parity inside phcc: 77/77 capabilities with C counterparts, 0 gaps (phext/PARITY.md).
- Conformance: 163,831 checks, 0 failures under gcc; 163,831 checks, 0 failures under phcc itself (dogfood).
- Differential fuzz: 40,000 cases, 0 divergences on defined behaviour.
- Local commit ready to push: 66ef47108f6580995a654a32e4ecb990b837420d (on top of 395f5d63).
- libphext-rs 0.5.0 parity: 93/93 capabilities with C counterparts, 0 gaps (phext/PARITY.md sections 5-7 + 0.5.0 outcome).
- Conformance: 163,955 checks plain / 163,987 with PHEXT_WITH_XZ, 0 failures under gcc AND under phcc itself (dogfood). Differential fuzz vs the published 0.5.0: 20,000 regression cases (ops 0-23) + 40,000 new cases (ops 24-38, binary payloads + seal cross-checks), 0 divergences, 0 Rust panics. Seal byte-identical to Rust's; C unseal of the shipped phcc.phext.xz reproduces phcc.phext byte-identically (the repo seal is the refresh tooling's preset 9-extreme stream, same format).
- Tree receipts on the final tree: make test ALL TESTS PASSED; conformance spot 332/333 (diverge set exactly [a_pp_018]); static gate cells 3/3. Phext refresh census: 613 manifest rows, 0 mismatches; scroll-diff vs base = exactly the 6 intended scrolls; WP receipt scroll (1.1.1/10.2.7/1.2.1) byte-identical, untouched.
- 0.5.0 move PUBLISHED 2026-11-08: wbic16/phcc main == exo == 53a15166; fresh-clone verification all green (phext hash, unpack 613/613, make test, parity 163,987/0 gcc+XZ and phcc, conformance 332/333, static cells 3/3).
# Make SQ and phext-shell handle the teixml 0.3 test outputs well

Coordinate: 41.10.8/10.10.14/12.9.13
Issued: 2026-11-14
Request (verbatim): TEI XML

https://teibyexample.org/exist/tools/software.htm
https://www.tei-c.org/tools/

We're going to provide users with a first-class upgrade from TEI-XML to Phextura. Using multiversal phext and standoff properties, encode all salient points of TEI-XML. Generate a fast Rust-based migrator called teixml-to-mutable.

Source: https://github.com/wbic16/teixml-to-mutable
Publish Target: crates.io
Output Formats: raw phext (0.1), mutable (0.2), phextura (0.3)

The goal is to help Ian populate content for Mutable OS at phext speed. Ask me any clarifying questions needed.
Status: COMPLETE 2026-11-14: SQ gap was deployment staleness only (node had Oct sq 0.6.0/libphext 0.3.3); sq 0.6.1 installed - counts exact (142,619/386,175/8,144), 1,800 sampled REST reads byte-identical incl. previously-capped coordinates. phext-shell 0.6.0 reads all three artifacts byte-identical (base 0.22s/128 MiB, standoff 0.91s/~694 MiB, image 1.92s/~1.49 GiB peak). One real defect found+fixed: REPL spun forever on stdin EOF - branch emise/shell-corpus-scale @ 343ebfe, PR https://github.com/wbic16/phext-shell/pull/6 open for Will; queue a phext-shell release task when it merges.

Notes:
- Will's words: 'make SQ and phext-shell handle the test outputs well' (2026-11-14 03:32 CST), spoken on merging teixml PR #3 + phextura PR #1.
- Record: ~/workspace/teixml-to-mutable-work/SQ-SHELL-E2E.md. Measured behavior noted, not changed: phext-shell 'lp' on the VFS image prints a ~533 MB transcript (libphext create_summary takes content to first break; VFS chunks are single-line 64 KiB base64).
Always use SHA-256 for checksums

Never MD5 or SHA-1 for file-integrity verification — they are insecure. Git's internal object IDs are identifiers git chooses, not checksums; when Emise verifies a file, she runs sha256sum.

