Results:
- Machine scroll at Design 1.1.1/3.2.3/1.1.2: 8 states / 25 events / 73 transitions / 9 invariants, derived from tccgen.c in the consolidated phext; 7 interpretation notes marked (N3: I3 rests mostly on mechanism + enumerated call-site discipline; N6: expr_cond parks its then-value off-stack).
- Static: tools/check_vstack.py PASS, 0 violations; 25/25 event functions resolve to Vol 3 def members of tccgen.c. First runs caught a checker regex defect (ev_gv2 dropped) and real scroll errors (vcheck_cmp materializes via gv(RC_INT), not gvtst_set) - scroll corrected to the code.
- Dynamic (ranch, phcc @ 8b56ea22): authored 26/26 PASS (24 model tests: model == phcc == gcc, traces legal vs the scroll; O01/O02 oracle-only phcc == gcc); tests2 corpus 24/24 match .expect. Trace tests at Tests 1.1.1/5.2.3/1.1.229-254.
- Regressions: 5 filed at Regressions 1.1.1/6.2.3/1.1.1-5, all Changelog-sourced (0.9.22:204 value stack full -> I1; 0.9.13:320 + 0.9.7:411 long long register spill -> I7; 0.9.10:359 lvalue type saved -> I7; 0.9.7:412 ?: register spill -> expr_cond save_regs).
- Gate v5.0.0: Slice 1-4 sections reproduce byte-identically on the base (baseline + machine-#2-absent block only); verdict at Meta 1.1.1/1.2.10/1.12.1 (sha 786fc893...), register at Sec 13, binding CURRENT; verdict reproduces byte-identically.
- Exit test PASS: vcheck_cmp() removed from vsetc in a scratch ranch copy -> exactly the 4 CMP-burying tests diverged (V06: 0 vs 1; V08: 1 vs 0; V09: 0 vs 10; V10: garbage vs 0 1 0 1), 22 others held; violated transition CMP --ev_check_cmp [...]--> REG named. V10 reclassified as burying by the exit test itself.
