Results:
- Branch emise/container-deploy @ b47aa5ef parented on exo 4b40fb45 (post-PR-#27 tree, fully token-free — grep-verified). 54 remote blobs + tree modes verified post-push. Files: Dockerfile (53 lines, repo root), .dockerignore, compose.yaml (61), deploy/container-entrypoint.sh (28, mode 100755), deploy/phext-edit.env.example (40, placeholders only), deploy/CONTAINER.md runbook (216), deploy.md +9 and readme.md +6 linking the new path.
- Design: multi-stage build (rust:1.94.0-bookworm runs deploy.sh's exact cargo build; runtime debian:bookworm-slim, binary + entrypoint + ca-certificates + curl), non-root user phext uid 10001, HEALTHCHECK on /api/session. Compose publishes 127.0.0.1:8080 only — host nginx unchanged, proxy contract documented incl. proxy_http_version 1.1 (SQ 403 rule). Entrypoint reproduces the production invocation with env overrides. deploy.sh path stays; runbook warns never to run both against the same data.
- Verified on aletheia-core (Docker 29.8.0, Compose v5.5.1): clean docker build; container healthy; / -> sign-in prompt; /api/session locked:true providers [github, google]; GitHub OAuth start 302 with correct redirect_uri; docker exec id = uid 10001; persistence proven — a scroll written via the real API in one container was present in the volume's phext after that container was removed, and the stack restarted healthy against it. Image 95,512,178 B.
- Findings: (1) no-new-privileges deliberately NOT in compose.yaml — snap-packaged Docker's AppArmor refused every exec with it set (bisected flag-by-flag; read_only + cap_drop ALL stay); reason + one-line re-enable documented in compose.yaml and the runbook. (2) Volume seeding must chown to uid 10001 or the server cannot write its library — runbook seed commands include it.
- REMAINING (Will's): merge the PR into exo; on the target host follow CONTAINER.md First run (fill phext-edit.env from the same values as /etc/phext-edit/oauth.env, seed the volume, compose up, confirm healthy). Host nginx needs no changes.
